"use strict";(self.webpackChunknowa_docs=self.webpackChunknowa_docs||[]).push([[6963],{88038:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"3-16-4","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-16-4","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-10-28-3-16-4.md","title":"Nowa 3.16.4: Faster Nowa AI and Multilingual Apps","description":"Nowa 3.16.4 makes Nowa AI faster and lighter on your credits, and lets you translate your app right on the board.","date":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.16.4: Faster Nowa AI and Multilingual Apps","sidebar_label":"3.16.4 \xb7 Faster AI, multilingual apps","description":"Nowa 3.16.4 makes Nowa AI faster and lighter on your credits, and lets you translate your app right on the board.","slug":"3-16-4","date":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","design","code"],"image":"/videos/whats-new/3.16.4-languages.jpg"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.16.1: Introducing Play-While-Edit","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-16-1"}},"content":"With Nowa 3.16.4, Nowa AI gets your requests done faster and with fewer credits, and you can translate your app right on the board. \ud83d\ude80\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## \u26a1 Nowa AI: faster, and lighter on your credits\\n\\nNowa AI now gets to the answer in fewer steps. It spends less time looking around your project and more time building, so your changes land sooner and each request uses fewer credits. Here\'s what changed:\\n\\n- **Fewer trips back and forth.** Nowa AI reads several files at once and gets small files whole. When a search finds just a few places, it gets the code around each one right away, instead of going back for more.\\n- **No reading the same code twice.** After an edit, it hears only what Nowa changed, instead of reading the whole file again, and when it explores your project it skips the code it has already seen.\\n- **Faster saves on cloud projects.** Each edit Nowa AI makes waits for one trip to our servers, instead of four or more.\\n\\nThere\'s something new it can do, too: ask Nowa AI to move or rename a file or a folder, and every import that points to it follows, in your code and in your tests.\\n\\nTaking on something big? **Deep Thinking**, the level for big features and tricky logic, now runs on Google\'s Gemini 4 Argon.\\n\\nNowa AI now needs Nowa 3.16.4 or later. If you\'re on an older version, the chat will ask you to update.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf0d Translate your app right on the board\\n\\nReach more people by speaking their language. Ask Nowa AI to add the languages you need, for example \\"Make my app available in English and Arabic\\", and it sets your app up the way Flutter recommends. Then you can see and polish every translation right on your board:\\n\\n- **See your screens in each language.** Click an empty spot on the board, then pick a **Language** under **All boards** in **Details**. Every board switches to it, and languages like Arabic flow right to left.\\n- **Add a language in a click.** Search the same list by a language\'s name, in English or in its own script, and click it.\\n- **Translate as you go.** Select a text and **Details** shows it in the language your boards show. A text that\'s still missing says **not translated**, so you know exactly what\'s left. Type the translation and press **Enter**, or double-click the text on the board, type over it and press **Esc**.\\n- **Make any text translatable.** For a text you typed straight into a widget, click **Translate** next to it in **Details**.\\n\\n<video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.16.4-languages.jpg\\">\\n  <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.16.4-languages.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n</video>\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc65 Bring all your GitHub accounts\\n\\nYour own repositories and your team\'s can now sit side by side. In the Git settings, under **GitHub Integration**, click **Add account** to connect another GitHub account. Each account shows whether it\'s personal or an organization and how many repositories Nowa can use, and **Manage** opens it on GitHub so you can pick them. See [Connect GitHub](/code/github#connect-github).\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf9e\ufe0f See your Lottie animations in the Library\\n\\nLottie animations in your assets now play right in their thumbnails in the **Library**, so you can find the one you want at a glance.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThat\'s the big stuff! \ud83d\udccb For every fix and smaller improvement, see the changelog for [3.16.4](/new/change-log#3164-28-october-2026), [3.16.3](/new/change-log#3163-25-october-2026) and [3.16.2](/new/change-log#3162-24-october-2026).\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear how the faster Nowa AI works for you. Click **?** at the bottom of the left sidebar and choose **Support** to message us, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-16-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-16-1","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-10-22-3-16-1.md","title":"Nowa 3.16.1: Introducing Play-While-Edit","description":"Nowa 3.16.1 introduces Play-While-Edit: play and edit your app at once, right inside the editor, with no build and no waiting.","date":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."},{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.16.1: Introducing Play-While-Edit","sidebar_label":"3.16.1 \xb7 Introducing Play-While-Edit","description":"Nowa 3.16.1 introduces Play-While-Edit: play and edit your app at once, right inside the editor, with no build and no waiting.","slug":"3-16-1","date":"2026-10-22T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["preview","integrations","nowa-ai","code"],"image":"/videos/whats-new/3.16.1-instant-play.jpg"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.16.4: Faster Nowa AI and Multilingual Apps","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-16-4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.15: Design right on the board","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-15"}},"content":"With Nowa 3.16.1, you can use your app and change it at the same time. \ud83d\ude80 Meet Play-While-Edit: your app plays right inside the editor with no build and no waiting, and you see your changes in it as you make them.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## \u25b6\ufe0f Play-While-Edit: play and edit your app at once\\n\\nYour app plays right where your board was, so you can test a flow, spot what\'s off and fix it, all without leaving your running app.\\n\\n### Play your app instantly\\n\\nClick the arrow next to **Run** and choose **Instant play**. Your app starts in a second, with nothing to build, so you can tap through your screens, fill in your forms and check every flow the way your users will. In the playground and in templates, just click **Run**.\\n\\n- **Check every screen size**: switch between **Phone**, **Tablet**, **Desktop** and **Full screen** in the top bar.\\n- **Start fresh**: click **Start over** to run your app from the beginning, as if you had just opened it.\\n- **Try one screen on its own**: click the screen\'s name next to the size, and pick the screen you want to play.\\n- **Hop back to your board** with the back arrow in the top bar. Forward takes you right back to your app.\\n\\n<video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.16.1-instant-play.jpg\\">\\n  <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.16.1-instant-play.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n</video>\\n\\n### Fix what you see, while it plays\\n\\nSpotted something that\'s off? Click **Select** in the top bar, or press **V**, and click it in your running app. Nowa outlines it just like on your board. Open **Details** beside your app to change its text, color or spacing, and watch your app update as you type. Hold **Shift** to pick a few things at once, and press **Esc** to go back to using your app.\\n\\nNowa AI sees what you pick, too. Select a button, ask the **Assistant** to \\"make this button bigger\\", and it knows exactly which button you mean.\\n\\n<video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.16.1-select-edit.jpg\\">\\n  <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.16.1-select-edit.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n</video>\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcac Get feedback right on your app\\n\\nClick **Comment**, or press **C**, then click anywhere on your app to leave a note exactly where it belongs. For a second opinion, click **Share** to copy a link to your app. The people on your project can open it in their browser, try your app and add their own comments, and if your project is public, anyone with the link can try it.\\n\\nEvery comment stays in your project, so nothing gets lost in chats or emails. **Resolve** a comment once it\'s handled, or click **Fix with AI** and let Nowa AI make the change it asks for.\\n\\n![Instant play with Comment turned on: two numbered pins sit on the running app, and the Comments panel beside it lists each note with Fix with AI and Resolve. Comment and Share are highlighted in the top bar](/img/whats_new/3.16.1-comments.png)\\n\\n## \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f All your data in one panel\\n\\n**Api**, **Firestore** and **Supabase** now live together in the new **Data** panel in the left sidebar, one tab each, and it opens on the tab you used last. Every tab works the same way: search to find what you need, connect right from the tab when something isn\'t connected yet, and point at an API request or a Supabase query or function to run it straight from the list.\\n\\n![The Data panel in the left sidebar, with its Api, Firestore and Supabase tabs, the search field, and the Run request button on a request highlighted](/img/whats_new/3.16.1-data-panel.png)\\n\\n## \ud83e\udded Help, right where you look for it\\n\\nHelp, your notifications and your account now sit together at the bottom of the left sidebar. Click **?** to read the docs, message our support team, look up a keyboard shortcut or book a call with a Nowa expert. Your project settings live down there too, and they open in a popup, so you never lose your place.\\n\\nLooking for the Router? Select a screen and click the route icon (**Open Router Editor**) under **Route Settings** in its **Details**.\\n\\n<img src=\\"/img/whats_new/3.16.1-sidebar-help.png\\" width=\\"408\\" alt=\\"The bottom of the left sidebar with the Help menu open: Docs, Talk to an expert, Support and Shortcuts, next to the notifications bell and the settings button\\" />\\n\\n## \ud83e\udd16 Nowa AI does more with your credits\\n\\n- **Longer chats for fewer credits**: Nowa AI now reads your project\'s overview, and any large screen or component you attach, only when your request needs it, instead of carrying it in every message. Long chats on big projects use noticeably fewer credits.\\n- **Your theme stays yours**: when you design with Nowa AI in an app you imported, it styles your screens with your app\'s own theme instead of adding a new one.\\n- **Packages without the extra step**: ask Nowa AI to add a package and it adds it, with no experimental setting to turn on first.\\n\\n---\\n\\nThat\'s the big stuff! \ud83d\udccb For every fix and smaller improvement in this release, see the [3.16.1 changelog](/new/change-log#3161-22-october-2026).\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear how Play-While-Edit works for you. Click **?** at the bottom of the left sidebar and choose **Support** to message us, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-15","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-15","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-10-20-3-15.md","title":"Nowa 3.15: Design right on the board","description":"Nowa 3.15 turns your board into a real design tool. Drag padding, gaps, corners and shadows right on your widgets, measure and line things up with familiar shortcuts, while a clearer Details panel tells you what each widget does.","date":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Account and teams","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/account","description":"Releases that changed your account, workspaces, organizations and the dashboard."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.15: Design right on the board","sidebar_label":"3.15 \xb7 Design right on the board","description":"Nowa 3.15 turns your board into a real design tool. Drag padding, gaps, corners and shadows right on your widgets, measure and line things up with familiar shortcuts, while a clearer Details panel tells you what each widget does.","slug":"3-15","date":"2026-10-20T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","nowa-ai","account","code"],"image":"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-board-handles.jpg"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.16.1: Introducing Play-While-Edit","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-16-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.14.1: A smoother road to the stores","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-14-1"}},"content":"Nowa 3.15 turns your board into a real design tool. \ud83c\udfa8 Drag padding, gaps, corners and shadows right on your widgets, measure and line things up with familiar shortcuts, while a clearer Details panel tells you what each widget does. The Themes panel can now edit any theme, Nowa AI shows its work in one live line and is much more reliable, and teams get organizations with shared workspaces and credits.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3150-20-october-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Design Right on the Board, Like in a Design Tool**\\n  Select a widget and shape it right where you see it:\\n  - **Padding and margins**: point at a widget\'s padding to see it, then drag its edge. Each padding and margin is its own ring, so you always know which one you\'re changing. New padding is still added in **Details**.\\n  - **Gaps**: drag the space between the children of a row, a column or a wrap.\\n  - **Corners, rotation and shadows**: drag the dot inside a corner to round the corners, turn a widget from just outside a corner, and drag a shadow to where it should fall. **Shift + H** and **Shift + V** flip a widget.\\n  - **Gradients**: right-click a widget with a gradient and choose **Edit gradient** to drag its ends and color stops.\\n\\n  Handles show their value as you drag, and the padding, gap and corner handles work on several widgets at once. A value that comes from your code, like a constant, shows as locked and tells you where it comes from.\\n\\n  <video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-board-handles.jpg\\">\\n    <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-board-handles.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n  </video>\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcd0 **Measure, Snap and Line Things Up**\\n  - **Sizes at a glance**: the size of your selection shows under it, with **Auto** or **Expand** when a side fits its content or fills the space.\\n  - **Measure**: hold **Alt** (**Option** on Mac) and point at another widget to see how far apart they are.\\n  - **Smarter snapping**: guides now show the distance to what you line up with, and widgets also snap to equal gaps, which are marked.\\n  - **Align and space**: for widgets placed freely, in a stack or on the board, familiar keys work, like **Alt + A** to align left and **Alt + Shift + H** to space three or more evenly (**Option** instead of **Alt** on Mac). Select a few and drag the gap between them to space them all the same.\\n  - **Auto layout**: press **Shift + A** to put the selected widgets in a row or a column, and **Shift + Alt + A** to turn a row or a column back into freely placed widgets.\\n\\n  <video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-measure-snap.jpg\\">\\n    <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-measure-snap.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n  </video>\\n\\n- \ud83e\udde9 **Components, Wrappers and Lists, the Way You Expect**\\n  - **Components work like instances in a design tool**: a component stays closed until you double-click it. While you edit it, the rest of the board dims, and **Done** in **Details** takes you back out.\\n  - **Wrappers at a glance**: a widget\'s wrappers, like a **Padding** or a **Container**, show as chips on top of it. Point at one to see what it adds, or hold **Ctrl** (**Control**, not Cmd, on Mac) to see every layer.\\n  - **Fewer wrappers**: turns and rounded image corners you add on the board go into one Container, and **Simplify wrappers** in the right-click menu folds an existing stack of wrappers into one.\\n  - **Lists**: click an item in a list to select that one, and the size label tells you which it is, like **2 of 3**.\\n\\n  <video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-components-wrappers.jpg\\">\\n    <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-components-wrappers.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n  </video>\\n\\n- \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f **A Details Panel That Explains Itself**\\n  Under a widget\'s name, **Details** now says what the code around it does, like *For each product in products* or *Shown when product.isNew*. Each wrapper is a tidy section with a one-line summary, like **Padding 16**, and a row\'s or column\'s padding now shows as a Padding wrapper too. Widgets with `@Preview` variants switch between them from the new **Variant** section.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **A Themes Panel That Edits Any Theme**\\n  The **Themes** panel now works with any theme, however it\'s written in your code, and tells you why when something can\'t be changed.\\n  - **Every widget\'s theme**: all of Flutter\'s widget themes, more than 50, grouped, searchable and each with a preview.\\n  - **Better text styles**: a real text style editor, and a picker that shows each style, with a tab for each theme extension.\\n  - **Quicker to use**: pickers open right beside the panel, color changes apply faster on big projects, and your boards use your project\'s own theme.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Nowa AI Shows Its Work, and Gets It Done**\\n  - **One live line**: while Nowa AI works, the chat shows one line that says what it\'s doing right now. When it\'s done, the line sums up what it did, like *Built the Login screen and updated the Home page*. Tap it to see every step and open what changed.\\n  - **Much more reliable**: the AI gets past connection hiccups on its own, keeps its work when you stop it or run out of credits, can check that the screens it builds show without errors on phones and tablets, and tells you when a change didn\'t save.\\n  - **Fewer credits for the same work**: it reads your project smarter and stops repeating itself, so tasks finish sooner and each message costs less.\\n  - **Safer with your app and data**: **Plan** mode can read your database but never changes your app, and with Supabase, the AI uses your connected tools and is more careful to keep your data private.\\n\\n  <video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-ai-activity-line.jpg\\">\\n    <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.15.0-ai-activity-line.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n  </video>\\n\\n- \ud83d\udc65 **Organizations for Teams**\\n  Teams on an organization plan can switch to their organization from the dashboard sidebar to share its workspaces, billing and AI credits. With your organization picked, the new **Organization** tab in your account settings handles seats, members, invites and roles.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcd6 **Your Code Stays as You Wrote It**\\n  When Nowa saves your code, it now keeps your annotations, like `@pragma` (so Firebase background messages keep working in release builds) and `@JsonSerializable`, and every `!` and `?.` right where you put them. **Copy as new widget** now makes code that compiles, and many false errors are gone, like the ones on dot shorthands, `clamp` and lists that mix kinds of items.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Smaller Touches**\\n  - **The Outline lives on your board**: the panels on your board fold into small chips, and the Outline opens right at the widget you selected.\\n  - **Shorter right-click menus**, grouped like a design tool\'s, with **Align**, **Flip** and **Edit gradient** right there.\\n  - **Clear credit limits**: when one request hits your plan\'s limit, Nowa pauses and tells you, and you can **Continue** with the credits you have left.\\n  - **Screens fix themselves**: a screen that failed to show comes back after your next change, and screens update as soon as Nowa AI edits them.\\n  - **The welcome tour** waits until Nowa AI has built your new app.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcbb **For Those Who Code**\\n  When you run your app on a device or simulator, the restart button shows when a reload is under way and why one failed, and edits from outside Nowa (like your own AI agent\'s) hot reload the running app. In local projects, the new **Run** page in your project settings holds your own `flutter run` arguments. In Git, the branch in the status bar marks local changes with `*` and syncs in one click, the branch menu shows how long ago each branch was last committed to, and in local projects a pull never overwrites your uncommitted changes.\\n\\n## **Bug Fixes \ud83e\ude79**\\n\\nWe fixed more than 45 bugs across the visual designer, saving your code, Nowa AI, the preview, the Themes panel, RevenueCat and Stripe on Android, Git, and updates on Windows. See every fix in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3150-20-october-2026).\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear how designing on the board feels now! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-14-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-14-1","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-10-15-3-14-1.md","title":"Nowa 3.14.1: A smoother road to the stores","description":"Nowa 3.14.1 makes designing faster and brings your app closer to the stores. The board now works like the design tools you know, with a zoom menu and familiar shortcuts, the Library can show your widgets as a grid of previews, and you can swap any widget for one you copied.","date":"2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Publish","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/publish","description":"Releases that changed deploying to the web and getting into the App Store and Google Play."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.14.1: A smoother road to the stores","sidebar_label":"3.14.1 \xb7 A smoother road to the stores","description":"Nowa 3.14.1 makes designing faster and brings your app closer to the stores. The board now works like the design tools you know, with a zoom menu and familiar shortcuts, the Library can show your widgets as a grid of previews, and you can swap any widget for one you copied.","slug":"3-14-1","date":"2026-10-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["publish","design","nowa-ai","code"],"image":"/videos/whats-new/3.14.1-agent-board-rows.jpg"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.15: Design right on the board","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-15"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.14: From idea to launch","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-14"}},"content":"Nowa 3.14.1 makes designing faster and brings your app closer to the stores. \ud83c\udfa8 The board now works like the design tools you know, with a zoom menu and familiar shortcuts, the Library can show your widgets as a grid of previews, and you can swap any widget for one you copied. Your app icons and Android builds are also readier for the App Store and Google Play, and your forms can check that two fields match.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3141-15-october-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfea **Smoother Road to the App Store and Google Play**\\n  - **App Store-ready icons**: Nowa gives your iOS app icon a white background, because Apple doesn\'t accept icons with transparency.\\n  - **Local notifications on Android**: apps that use them build for Android right away. Nowa adds the setting they need for you.\\n  - **AdMob reminders**: Nowa tells you when AdMob is missing its Android or iOS App ID, and takes you to its settings.\\n  - **SHA-1 keys**: paste them into Firebase Authentication with or without colons.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcdd **Better Forms and Data**\\n  - **\\"Must match\\" check**: make sure two fields match, like **Repeat password** and the password. Select the field, open its validator in **Details**, click **+ Add validator** and choose **Must match validator**. See [Check what people type](/reference/widgets/forms#validators).\\n  - **Default values**: models built from your API use the defaults you set when a response leaves a field out.\\n  - **Supabase**: your create and update functions send only the fields you filled in.\\n\\n  ![The + Add validator menu of a Text Field\'s validator in Details, with Min length, Max length, Email, Phone, Regex and the new Must match validator (highlighted)](/img/whats_new/3.14.1-must-match.png)\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Move Around Your Board Like in a Design Tool**\\n  - **A zoom menu**: click the zoom level in the board toolbar to zoom in or out, fit everything, zoom to your selection or go back to 100%.\\n  - **Familiar shortcuts**: **+** and **-** zoom in and out, **Shift + 1** fits everything, **Shift + 2** zooms to your selection and **Shift + 0** goes to 100%. Double-click to go one layer deeper, press **Enter** to select the layers inside, and press **Shift + Enter** or **Esc** to go back up. See [Keyboard shortcuts](/reference/shortcuts).\\n  - **Clear layer names**: the Outline names each layer by what it shows, such as an icon\'s name or an image\'s file.\\n\\n  ![The board toolbar with its zoom level (100%) clicked: a menu above it lists Zoom in (+), Zoom out (-), Zoom to fit (Shift 1), Zoom to selection (Shift 2) and Zoom to 100% (Shift 0)](/img/whats_new/3.14.1-zoom-menu.png)\\n\\n- \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f **See Your Library as a Grid**\\n  Open the **View** menu at the top of the Library and choose **Grid** to see your widgets as a grid of previews. Choose **Tree** or **List** to switch back. See [Find and add things with the Library](/design/library).\\n\\n  ![The Library in Grid view, with the View menu open (Tree, List, Grid checked) and the Built-in widgets shown as previews: Button, Icon Button and Floating Button under Buttons, then Checkbox and Switch under Forms](/img/whats_new/3.14.1-library-grid.png)\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd01 **Paste to Replace**\\n  Copy a widget, right-click another one and choose **Paste to replace**. Your copy takes its place and keeps its layout, and one undo brings the old one back.\\n\\n  ![The right-click menu of a text widget on a screen, with Paste to replace (highlighted) right after Cut](/img/whats_new/3.14.1-paste-to-replace.png)\\n\\n- \u270f\ufe0f **Quicker Edits**\\n  - **Paste SVGs from anywhere**: an SVG copied from another app or a website becomes an image in your assets.\\n  - **Arrow keys in number fields**: press **Up** or **Down** to change a value like the width by 1, or hold **Shift** to change it by 10.\\n  - **New screens appear in the middle** of your view.\\n  - **Text shows its real font and size** in **Details**, including the ones that come from your theme.\\n  - **Undo a rename**: renaming a component in **Details** can be undone like any other change.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Smarter AI Help**\\n  - **Several widgets at once**: select a few widgets and ask Nowa AI for a change, and it changes all of them.\\n  - **Keeps going on its own**: if the connection goes quiet in the middle of a task, Nowa AI picks it up again by itself.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Smaller Touches**\\n  - **Smoother updates on Mac**: Nowa puts the new version in place before it restarts.\\n  - **Menus show every entry**, up to the height of your screen.\\n  - **Copy from help**: you can select and copy the text in help popups, handy for IDs and keys.\\n  - **Faster Library previews** when you point at a widget.\\n  - **Clearer Circuit steps**: each step shows what it acts on, such as `emailController.clear`, so similar steps are easy to tell apart.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udd1d **Your Own AI Agent, Working With Your Team**\\n  When you connect Claude Code, Claude Desktop or Cursor to Nowa and design in your team\'s UI package (a package that holds your team\'s widgets and screens, without an app of its own), your agent works the way a designer would:\\n  - **A tidy board**: each screen and component lands on your board in its own row, with its states (such as Loading, Empty and Error) beside it and, for a screen, its prototype at the end. Your agent checks every state before it says it\'s done.\\n  - **Sample data stays out of your app**: previews, sample data and prototypes go to a `design/` folder, so your app only ships the real widgets.\\n  - **You stay in control**: Nowa asks you before your agent changes a file outside the package, like your developers\' app. Click **Allow** or **Cancel**.\\n  - **Builds on the first try**: fonts and components your agent adds work in your team\'s app right away.\\n\\n  Connecting your own agent is **Enterprise only**. See [Connect your own AI agent](/ai/external-agent).\\n\\n  <video controls playsInline preload=\\"metadata\\" width=\\"100%\\" poster=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.14.1-agent-board-rows.jpg\\">\\n    <source src=\\"/videos/whats-new/3.14.1-agent-board-rows.mp4\\" type=\\"video/mp4\\" />\\n  </video>\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcbb **For Those Who Code**\\n  Clone a cloud project to your computer without installing Flutter first, and the Git panel picks up commits and branch changes you make outside Nowa as soon as you come back. In code mode, right-click a folder to create a file or folder inside it, and Nowa offers a one-click fix when you `await` a function that\'s no longer async.\\n\\n## **Bug Fixes \ud83e\ude79**\\n\\nWe fixed more than 30 bugs across the visual designer and board, the Outline, forms and validators, Nowa AI and connected agents, Firebase, Supabase, Android builds, Play mode, sending feedback and updates on Mac. See every fix in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3141-15-october-2026).\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear how the new board feels! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-14","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-14","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-10-13-3-14.md","title":"Nowa 3.14: From idea to launch","description":"Nowa 3.14 helps you take your app from idea to launch. We tested Nowa intensively and polished it from end to end, focusing on what matters most for a real product: your data, your payments, and getting into the App Store and Google Play.","date":"2026-10-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Publish","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/publish","description":"Releases that changed deploying to the web and getting into the App Store and Google Play."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.14: From idea to launch","sidebar_label":"3.14 \xb7 From idea to launch","description":"Nowa 3.14 helps you take your app from idea to launch. We tested Nowa intensively and polished it from end to end, focusing on what matters most for a real product: your data, your payments, and getting into the App Store and Google Play.","slug":"3-14","date":"2026-10-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations","publish","design","nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.14.1: A smoother road to the stores","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-14-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.13: Your whole project in one Library","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-13"}},"content":"Nowa 3.14 helps you take your app from idea to launch. \ud83d\ude80 We tested Nowa intensively and polished it from end to end, focusing on what matters most for a real product: your data, your payments, and getting into the App Store and Google Play. Our docs are also brand new, with a guide for every step, and Nowa now runs on Linux too. \ud83d\udc27\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3140-13-october-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcda **Brand-New Docs**\\n  We rewrote our docs from scratch. They now cover everything you need to build a great app with Nowa, from A to Z. Start with the new [Build a great app](/guides) section for tips and tricks, then explore Nowa AI, Firebase (including push notifications), payments, maps, ads, and step-by-step publishing to Google Play and the App Store. [Check them out](/)!\\n\\n- \ud83d\udc27 **Nowa Is on Linux**\\n  The Nowa desktop app now runs on Linux, alongside Mac and Windows, so you can build on whichever computer you prefer. Download the 64-bit version, and the install script adds Nowa to your app menu for you. [Get it here](/get-started/desktop-app).\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd25 **Build Your Database Visually**\\n  The new **Firestore** panel in the left sidebar shows all your collections and queries. Add a collection or a query in one click, and build queries that add and read documents without writing any code. See [Firestore](/integrations/firebase/firestore).\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfea **Ready for the App Store and Google Play**\\n  - **Account deletion**: Apple and Google require apps with sign-up to let people delete their account. Firebase Authentication now adds this for you.\\n  - **Restore purchases**: new RevenueCat projects include it, so subscribers keep what they paid for on a new phone.\\n  - **iOS builds** always use your app\'s latest bundle ID.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcb3 **Ready to Get Paid**\\n  Switch Google Pay from **Test** to **Production** with the new **Environment** setting in Stripe, and start taking real payments. Your own changes to the payment code stay in place when Nowa updates it.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd10 **A Secure Backend by Default**\\n  Nowa deploys your Supabase edge functions with Supabase\'s security check turned on. Only Stripe\'s webhook stays public, and the setup summary shows which functions are public.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Easier Visual Building**\\n  - **Widgets fit their content** on the board, the same as in your app.\\n  - **App bars, floating buttons, bottom navigation bars and drawers** go straight to the right place when you drop them on a screen.\\n  - **Templates** add the packages they need.\\n  - **Renaming an image** updates every widget that uses it.\\n  - **New sliders** use your theme\'s colors, and the **Empty Page** template lets you pick a device size.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Smarter AI Help**\\n  - **Restore Checkpoint** shows how many AI requests it will undo.\\n  - **Fix with AI** knows which step of your Supabase setup needs attention.\\n  - **Explain with AI** gives clearer answers about your build logs.\\n  - **Attach text files** to the AI chat on the web too.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd17 **Deep Links Open the Right Screen**\\n  A link from an email, an ad or a message now opens the right screen in your app.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Smaller Touches**\\n  - **Lighter on your computer**: Nowa now uses much less memory.\\n  - **A fresh look**: menus share one clean design with built-in search.\\n  - **Sample data while you design**: the board shows sample responses for your API requests, so your live data isn\'t touched.\\n  - **View Only members** can copy widgets and export them as images.\\n  - **Clearer messages** that stay on screen longer.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcbb **For Those Who Code**\\n  Nowa keeps your code, comments and formatting the way you wrote them. Local projects also support SSH keys and easier Git conflict resolution.\\n\\n## **Bug Fixes \ud83e\ude79**\\n\\nWe fixed more than 150 bugs across the visual designer and board, the Library, Nowa AI, Firebase, Supabase, Stripe and RevenueCat, REST APIs, navigation and deep links, Instant Play and sharing, publishing and cloud builds, Git and local projects, and the desktop app. See every fix in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3140-13-october-2026).\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear how Nowa 3.14 feels! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-13","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-13","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-10-06-3-13.md","title":"Nowa 3.13: Your whole project in one Library","description":"Nowa 3.13 gives everything in your project one home: the new Library. Find any screen, component or widget in a few keystrokes and add it to your board without reaching for the mouse.","date":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.13: Your whole project in one Library","sidebar_label":"3.13 \xb7 Your whole project in one Library","description":"Nowa 3.13 gives everything in your project one home: the new Library. Find any screen, component or widget in a few keystrokes and add it to your board without reaching for the mouse.","slug":"3-13","date":"2026-10-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.14: From idea to launch","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-14"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.12.5: Big boards, up to 50x faster","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12-5"}},"content":"Nowa 3.13 gives everything in your project one home: the new **Library**. \ud83d\udcda Find any screen, component or widget in a few keystrokes and add it to your board without reaching for the mouse. This release also brings a desktop app for Linux, quicker ways to move around your project, and your theme extension colors right in the color picker.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3130-6-october-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcda **The Library: Your Whole Project in One Place**\\n  The **Library** replaces the Widgets panel. Your screens, components, models and global states, Nowa\'s built-in widgets, the widgets in your packages and your assets now live in one searchable list.\\n  - **Add anything fast**: press **Ctrl/Cmd + K** (or click the **Widget** tool), type what you need and press **Enter** to drop it on your board.\\n  - **Go anywhere**: press **Ctrl/Cmd + O**, type a name and press **Enter** to open it.\\n  - **Find your way around**: filter by kind, choose which of your project, packages, built-in widgets and assets to show, and jump straight to the code with **Show in code**.\\n\\n  **Files** now lives in code mode only, where you can move through your project with the keyboard and drag several files into a folder at once. Learn more in [Find and add things with the Library](/design/library).\\n\\n- \u2194\ufe0f **Back, Forward and All Your Boards**\\n  Two new arrows in the top bar take you back and forward through the screens and files you\'ve opened, just like in a browser (**Ctrl + -** and **Ctrl + Shift + -**, with Control on macOS too). The board chip now lists every board in your project: press **Ctrl/Cmd + B**, type a name and press **Enter**, or create a new board right from the list.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udc27 **Nowa for Linux**\\n  Nowa now has a desktop app for Linux. Choose **Linux** when you download Nowa to get a 64-bit archive with an install script that adds Nowa to your app menu. On Linux, you download updates from the update dialog, and your app\'s preview opens in your browser. See [Install the desktop app](/get-started/desktop-app).\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Your Theme Extensions in the Pickers**\\n  If your theme uses theme extensions, the color picker now shows a tab for each one next to **Material**, and the text style picker lists their styles in their own groups. Pick a color and Nowa links it to your extension for you. See [Edit theme extensions](/design/themes#edit-theme-extensions).\\n\\n- \ud83e\udde9 **Widget Variants from `@Preview`**\\n  Add Flutter\'s `@Preview` to a function or constructor that builds your widget, and Nowa shows it as a named variant: next to the component when you open it, as a choice in the widget picker, and under the widget in the Library. See [Preview a widget in several states](/code/custom-code#preview-variants).\\n\\n- \ud83d\udce6 **More of Your Code and Packages Just Work**\\n  - **Packages**: `git:` and `path:` dependencies now load in local projects, `sdk:` dependencies like `flutter_localizations` count as installed, and `gap`, `flutter_animate`, `google_fonts` and `smooth_page_indicator` now work on the board.\\n  - **Your own Flutter code**: much more hand-written code renders on the board, including switch patterns like `> 5`, named arguments passed to `super(...)`, and `part` files, which now stay intact when Nowa saves. Screens from open-source apps like Flutter\'s compass_app and Wonderous render too.\\n  - **Smarter placeholders**: a package widget Nowa can\'t draw is now a small box, and one that wraps another widget shows what it wraps.\\n  - **Page indicators**: `nowa_runtime` no longer includes `smooth_page_indicator`. If your project uses page dots, Nowa offers to add the package to your pubspec in one click (**Migrate**).\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcbb **Local Projects Stay in Sync**\\n  Changes you make in another editor right after Nowa saves are no longer missed, and new dependencies you add to `pubspec.yaml` outside Nowa load on their own.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Smaller Touches**\\n  - **A fresh look**: new buttons, lists and menus throughout, and the Albert Sans font is back.\\n  - **Design-tool words**: **Bring forward**, **Send backward**, **Bring to front** and **Send to back** replace the old move entries. **Ctrl/Cmd + Alt/Option + ]** or **[** moves a widget all the way to the front or back.\\n  - **Default in dropdowns**: the dropdown of a property that can be left empty now starts with **Default**, which keeps the widget\'s own default.\\n  - **Branch search**: find a Git branch by typing in the branch menu.\\n  - **Tidier boards**: each screen stays inside its frame, and snap guides line up at any zoom.\\n  - **Quieter Git history**: opening a project in a newer Nowa no longer changes `.nowa/settings.json`.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f Tell us how the Library feels! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-12-5","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12-5","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-09-25-3-12-5.md","title":"Nowa 3.12.5: Big boards, up to 50x faster","description":"Nowa 3.12.5 makes big projects feel light again. Boards with lots of screens are now up to 50x faster to move around and work in, projects reopen faster, and Instant Play can now play anything on your board.","date":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.12.5: Big boards, up to 50x faster","sidebar_label":"3.12.5 \xb7 Big boards, up to 50x faster","description":"Nowa 3.12.5 makes big projects feel light again. Boards with lots of screens are now up to 50x faster to move around and work in, projects reopen faster, and Instant Play can now play anything on your board.","slug":"3-12-5","date":"2026-09-25T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","preview","code","nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.13: Your whole project in one Library","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-13"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.12.3: Nowa AI now works with Figma","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12-3"}},"content":"Nowa 3.12.5 makes big projects feel light again. \u26a1 Boards with lots of screens are now **up to 50x faster** to move around and work in, projects reopen faster, and Instant Play can now play anything on your board. This release also lets you switch Git branches without committing first, gives your connected agent a way to bring images (including the ones in your Figma designs) into your project, and helps Nowa understand even more of the Flutter code you write yourself.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3125-25-september-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \u26a1 **Big Boards, Up to 50x Faster**\\n  Nowa no longer runs every screen on your board at once. Instead, it puts its effort where you are:\\n  - **What you\'re looking at loads first.** Screens build one at a time, starting with the ones in view, so a big board opens without freezing the editor.\\n  - **Only the screen you\'re working on keeps moving.** Animations and timers run on the screen you\'re hovering, selecting or playing, and pause everywhere else.\\n  - **Screens out of view wait.** Changes to screens you\'ve scrolled away from are applied when you come back to them.\\n  - **Crowded views stay smooth.** When lots of screens are in view at once, the ones you\'re not working on are shown as a still picture until you need them.\\n\\n  Reopening a project is faster too: Nowa now keeps its analysis of the packages your project uses, instead of redoing it every time you open the project.\\n\\n- \u25b6\ufe0f **Play Anything on Your Board**\\n  Instant Play now works on any item on your board, not only screens and components. Right-click any widget and choose **Play** to play the item it belongs to. While something is playing, just select another item to play that one instead.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udf3f **Switch Branches Without Committing First**\\n  You no longer have to commit or discard your work before changing branches. Switch or create a branch and your changes come with you. If they touch files that are different on the other branch, Nowa asks before bringing them along, and if anything clashes, it opens the conflict resolver so you choose what to keep. Any unsaved edits are saved before the switch, so nothing gets left behind.\\n\\n- \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f **Your Connected Agent Can Add Images**\\n  Claude Code, Claude Desktop, and Cursor can now add images to your project. Your agent hands Nowa image links, like the ones it gets from Figma\'s own MCP, or files from your computer, and Nowa downloads them into `assets/images/` and registers them for you. PNG, JPG, GIF, WebP, BMP and SVG all work.\\n\\n  Connecting your own agent is still **Enterprise only**. If you\'d like access, email us at `team@nowa.dev` and we\'ll get you set up.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcd6 **Nowa Understands Even More of Your Code**\\n  More of the Flutter code you bring into Nowa now renders on the board just the way you wrote it:\\n  - **More packages**: `equatable`, `auto_size_text`, and `package:collection` helpers like `mapIndexed` and `flattened`.\\n  - **Projects exported from FlutterFlow**: pages using `safeSetState`, custom functions, and Firestore records now render with placeholder data, even without a Firebase connection on the board.\\n  - **Smarter placeholders**: a widget Nowa has no value for now shows as a small slot, instead of taking over your layout.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Smaller Touches**\\n  - **More precise snapping** when you move or resize widgets, and resizing only snaps the edge you\'re dragging.\\n  - **A lighter Widgets panel**: previews play their animations for a moment, then settle.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear how your biggest projects feel now! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-12-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12-3","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-09-22-3-12-3.md","title":"Nowa 3.12.3: Nowa AI now works with Figma","description":"Nowa AI now works with Figma! Connect your Figma account and the AI can bring your images, icons, colors and text styles straight into your project, so the app you build matches the design you made.","date":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.12.3: Nowa AI now works with Figma","sidebar_label":"3.12.3 \xb7 Nowa AI now works with Figma","description":"Nowa AI now works with Figma! Connect your Figma account and the AI can bring your images, icons, colors and text styles straight into your project, so the app you build matches the design you made.","slug":"3-12-3","date":"2026-09-22T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","code","design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.12.5: Big boards, up to 50x faster","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12-5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.12: Connect your own AI agent","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12"}},"content":"Nowa AI now works with **Figma**! \ud83c\udfa8 Connect your Figma account and the AI can bring your images, icons, colors and text styles straight into your project, so the app you build matches the design you made. The Figma MCP has been on our \\"coming soon\\" list for a while, and now it\'s here for everyone. This release also helps Nowa understand much more of the Flutter code you write yourself, cuts down on false alarms, and makes the board smoother to move around.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3123-22-september-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Figma MCP Is Here**\\n  Nowa AI can now connect to your Figma account and work with your designs. Once it\'s connected, just ask, and the AI can:\\n  - **Bring in your images and icons** as project assets, SVGs included.\\n  - **Turn your Figma colors and text styles into your app\'s theme**, so every screen stays true to your design.\\n\\n  To connect, click the **Figma icon** in the AI chat, right next to the Supabase one, and approve access in the browser window that opens. That\'s it! You can connect or disconnect anytime from **Account Details \u2192 Connected Accounts** in your account settings. Figma works in both cloud and local projects, and the AI asks for your OK before each Figma action unless you turn on **Auto-approve tools** from the Figma icon\'s menu.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcd6 **Nowa Understands More of Your Code**\\n  Bringing your own Flutter project into Nowa? Much more of it now opens and renders on the board just the way you wrote it, including:\\n  - **Modern Dart patterns**, like `switch` expressions that match on records and objects, and destructuring.\\n  - **Widgets that build on other widgets**, whether they\'re your own (even from another file) or Flutter\'s, with `super.` parameters passing their values along.\\n  - **InheritedWidgets, mixins, enhanced enums and redirecting constructors**, all working the way you\'d expect.\\n  - **Up to 8 theme extensions** in your theme, up from 5.\\n\\n  And when Nowa meets a piece of code it can\'t read yet, it now skips just that part and tells you about it in the Problems panel, instead of giving up on the whole file.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd0d **Fewer False Alarms, Clearer Answers**\\n  Nowa is now better at telling a real problem from perfectly good code, and at telling you what to do next:\\n  - Projects without a `main.dart` or a `web/` folder, like packages or mobile-only apps, are no longer flagged as broken.\\n  - If the in-app preview can\'t run your app, Nowa explains why as soon as you hit **Run**. When all it needs is web support, one click on **Add web support** sets it up for you.\\n  - The **Problems panel** waits for your packages to finish loading before it reports anything, and lists any package that didn\'t load along with the reason.\\n  - A new filter in the Problems panel lets you check **All files**, not just the code Nowa generated.\\n\\n- \u26a1 **A Smoother Board**\\n  Panning and zooming around the board feel smoother, and Nowa does less work behind the scenes as your project loads and as you edit. You\'ll notice it most in bigger projects.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd0c **More Power for Your Connected Agent**\\n  Using Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or Cursor with Nowa? Your agent just got better at the job:\\n  - **Connecting takes one command.** The **Connect External Agent** dialog now gives you a ready-made Claude Code command to copy and run.\\n  - **It can set app permissions**, like camera or location access, the same way the Permissions panel does.\\n  - **It knows Nowa\'s building rules** from the moment it connects, so its changes fit right in.\\n  - **It can see layout problems.** Screenshots now tell it about overflows and widgets that failed to build, so it can catch and fix them itself.\\n  - **Its edits are safer.** Code that doesn\'t parse is refused instead of saved, and an edit can\'t land on the wrong widget if the design changed in the meantime.\\n\\n  Connecting your own agent is still **Enterprise only**. If you\'d like access, email us at `team@nowa.dev` and we\'ll get you set up.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We can\'t wait to see what you build from your Figma designs! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-12","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-09-15-3-12.md","title":"Nowa 3.12: Connect your own AI agent","description":"Nowa 3.12 lets your AI coding agent work inside your project. Connect Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or Cursor to Nowa and it can open your projects, see what\'s on your canvas, and build using Nowa\'s own tools while your board updates in front of you.","date":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Account and teams","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/account","description":"Releases that changed your account, workspaces, organizations and the dashboard."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.12: Connect your own AI agent","sidebar_label":"3.12 \xb7 Connect your own AI agent","description":"Nowa 3.12 lets your AI coding agent work inside your project. Connect Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or Cursor to Nowa and it can open your projects, see what\'s on your canvas, and build using Nowa\'s own tools while your board updates in front of you.","slug":"3-12","date":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","code","account"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.12.3: Nowa AI now works with Figma","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12-3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.11.5: Smarter context, better designs","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-11-5"}},"content":"Nowa 3.12 lets your AI coding agent work inside your project. Connect **Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or Cursor** to Nowa and it can open your projects, see what\'s on your canvas, and build using Nowa\'s own tools while your board updates in front of you. \ud83d\udd0c This release also adds **workspace and monorepo support**, **Sign in with Apple**, **Git over SSH**, and a tidier interface throughout.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3120-15-september-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd0c **Connect Your Own AI Agent**\\n  The Nowa desktop app can now talk to the coding agent you already use: **Claude Code, Claude Desktop, or Cursor**. Once it\'s connected, your agent can:\\n  - **Open and switch between your projects** by name.\\n  - **See what you see**: your screens and components, your theme and colours, the widget tree, and whatever you have selected on the canvas.\\n  - **Build with Nowa\'s own tools**, so every change it makes is a real Nowa change and your board keeps up as it works.\\n  - **Point at things visually.** Ask it to open a screen, highlight a widget, take a screenshot of the canvas, or save your project.\\n\\n  This one is **Enterprise only for now**. If you\'d like access, email us at `team@nowa.dev` and we\'ll get you set up.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udce6 **Workspaces & Monorepos**\\n  Nowa can now open a Flutter app that lives inside a bigger repository. When you import a local project, Nowa reads the folder and lets you choose which package to edit. Once you\'re inside, a chip in the top bar switches between packages without leaving the project, and Git still covers the whole repository, so nothing about your setup has to change.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udf4e **Sign in with Apple**\\n  You can now sign in to Nowa with your Apple ID on the web and on iOS, alongside Google and email.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd11 **Git over SSH**\\n  Local projects can now push and pull over SSH. Point Nowa at a key, or let it use the keys already loaded in your ssh-agent, so the setup you use in the terminal works here too.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcdd **Describe Your Components**\\n  Your screens and components can now carry a short description, written in the details panel right next to their fields. It\'s a quick way to leave a note for your teammates, and for the AI, about what a component is for.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd17 **Share a Preview of One Screen**\\n  Hit play on a screen from the board and the share link now opens on that exact screen, so whoever you send it to lands where you wanted them to.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udded **Go to Definition in the Code Editor**\\n  Hold **\u2318 (or Ctrl)** and the name under your cursor turns into a link. Click it to jump straight to where it\'s defined.\\n\\n- \u2728 **A Tidier Interface**\\n  We rebuilt the top bar and cleaned up the dashboard. A few smaller touches come with it:\\n  - Switching to code mode now takes you to the code behind the widget you had selected, instead of the top of the file.\\n  - Run and preview controls stay with you in code mode, so you don\'t have to switch back to play your app.\\n  - The diff view has a navigator for moving between changes, so you\'re not scrolling to find them.\\n  - Widgets that offer more than one constructor now let you pick the one you want.\\n  - Cloning a project from GitHub shows progress, so it no longer looks stuck.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfaf **Code That Looks Like Yours**\\n  Nowa now follows your project\'s own formatting rules from `analysis_options.yaml`. Files it saves come back in the shape your project already uses, so your diffs only show what actually changed.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udde9 **Custom App Bars**\\n  Your own widgets can now be used as a screen\'s app bar, so a custom header you built once works everywhere a Flutter app bar does.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear what you think of Nowa 3.12! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-11-5","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-11-5","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-08-23-3-11-5.md","title":"Nowa 3.11.5: Smarter context, better designs","description":"Smart context cleaning cuts the credits your prompts use by up to 75% in long sessions, Design mode is now the best place to start a new project, and running your app is more reliable.","date":"2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.11.5: Smarter context, better designs","sidebar_label":"3.11.5 \xb7 Smarter context, better designs","description":"Smart context cleaning cuts the credits your prompts use by up to 75% in long sessions, Design mode is now the best place to start a new project, and running your app is more reliable.","slug":"3-11-5","date":"2026-08-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","design","preview"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.12: Connect your own AI agent","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-12"},"nextItem":{"title":"Design mode","permalink":"/new/whats-new/design-mode"}},"content":"Nowa 3.11.5 only moves the version number a little, but what\'s inside is not small at all. \ud83e\uddf9 Smart context cleaning cuts the credits your prompts use by up to 75% in long sessions, Design mode is now the best place to start a new project, and running your app is more reliable.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83e\uddf9 **Way Fewer Credits with Smart Context Cleaning**\\n  When a chat with the AI gets long, older parts of the conversation get sent along with every new message. Every prompt gets more expensive, and the AI starts losing focus. Now, as the session grows, the agent removes the parts of the old context it no longer needs, while keeping everything that matters for the results and the overall picture of your app.\\n  - **Up to 75% fewer credits per prompt**: in our testing, sessions that go beyond three or four prompts saw credit usage drop by up to 75%.\\n  - **Faster, better results**: tasks run faster, and the AI stays focused on what actually matters.\\n\\n  If the previous history isn\'t needed for your next task, starting a fresh chat is still the best way to go.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Design Mode Is the Best Place to Start a New Project**\\n  We now recommend starting every new project in **Design** mode. It follows the natural flow of building an app: you start with the design, focus fully on your screens and how people move through them, and leave the logic for later.\\n  - **Better designs**: Design mode is now much more capable of creating modern designs that feel unique to your app instead of looking like a template.\\n  - **Five questions first**: before it starts building, it asks about the look and feel, the tone, the user experience and how the app flows from one screen to the next. For the questions about user experience and flow, it highlights a recommended answer.\\n  - **Smarter next steps**: once the first version of the design is ready, it\'s smarter about suggesting what to do next.\\n\\n- \u25b6\ufe0f **Running Your App Is More Reliable**\\n  Some of you saw the app fail to run for no clear reason, most of the time because the simulator was still booting while the AI was in the middle of its work. Now your simulator only shows an error or fails to run if your project actually contains errors, and you can fix them with **one click using AI**.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Smaller Touches**\\n  - **Uploaded images make it into your app**: the AI adds the images you upload to your project\'s assets and uses them on its own.\\n  - **A smarter AI agent**: it explores your project and edits files better, for better results, lower cost and faster execution.\\n  - **A better support chat**: the support chat panel got a round of improvements.\\n\\nRead the full story in [Nowa 3.11.5: Smarter Context, Better Designs, and a Bunch of Fixes](https://nowa.dev/blog/nowa-3-11-5-release/) on our blog.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We can\'t wait to see what you build with this version! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"design-mode","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/design-mode","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-08-20-design-mode.md","title":"Design mode","description":"Design mode is a new Nowa AI mode that does one thing only: design. It asks about your users and your style before it draws a single screen, and it never touches logic or real data.","date":"2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Design mode","sidebar_label":"Design mode","description":"Design mode is a new Nowa AI mode that does one thing only: design. It asks about your users and your style before it draws a single screen, and it never touches logic or real data.","slug":"design-mode","date":"2026-08-20T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.11.5: Smarter context, better designs","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-11-5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Gemini 3.7 Flash upgrade","permalink":"/new/whats-new/gemini-3-7-flash"}},"content":"We\'re excited to introduce **Design mode**, a new Nowa AI mode that does one thing only: design. \ud83c\udfa8 It asks about your users and your style before it draws a single screen, and it never touches logic or real data.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n<iframe width=\\"767\\" height=\\"431\\" src=\\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/t8y5S2T7O1A\\" title=\\"Meet the Design Agent | Design Stunning Apps with AI, Before Any Logic\\" frameborder=\\"0\\" allow=\\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\\" referrerpolicy=\\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\\n\\n## **How It Works \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Pure Design, Sample Data, No Logic**\\n  Until now, Agent mode did everything at once: the design, the logic and the data. That works, but when an agent thinks about all of that at the same time, the design often suffers. So design got its own mode. Design mode won\'t write logic and won\'t use real data. Its whole job is how your app looks and feels, and how people move through it.\\n\\n- \u2753 **It Asks Before It Draws**\\n  Tell it about your app, and before it draws anything, it asks a few questions, the way good designers do:\\n  - **Who will use the app?** The screens change completely depending on who\'s holding the phone.\\n  - **What look do you want?** Playful, serious, minimal: the whole style follows from this.\\n  - **How should people move through it?** Where they land, what they tap next, where they end up.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udded **The Workflow We Suggest**\\n  - **Start a project in Design mode**: describe your app the way you\'d describe it to a friend.\\n  - **Answer its questions**: they\'re all about design and how people will use the app, nothing about code.\\n  - **Ask for a few versions if you\'re unsure**: it makes 2 or 3 versions of your main screen and puts them on the board. Pick the one you like, and it deletes the rest and designs your other screens in that style.\\n  - **Make one part real**: when it\'s done, it suggests next steps. Keep working on the design, or pick one part of the app to make real, and Nowa switches to Agent mode to build that part.\\n\\n- \ud83e\uddea **Nothing to Break**\\n  There\'s no logic behind anything yet, so you can play around without worry. Move stuff around and change your mind. Nothing breaks.\\n\\nLearn how to use it in [Design, Plan and Agent modes](/ai/modes#design-mode), and read the full story in [Introducing Designer Mode](https://nowa.dev/blog/introducing-designer-mode/) on our blog.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If something feels off or confusing, tell us! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"gemini-3-7-flash","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/gemini-3-7-flash","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-08-13-gemini-3-7-flash.md","title":"Gemini 3.7 Flash upgrade","description":"Google released Gemini 3.7 Flash today, and Nowa\'s AI agent is already running on it.","date":"2026-08-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Gemini 3.7 Flash upgrade","sidebar_label":"Gemini 3.7 Flash upgrade","description":"Google released Gemini 3.7 Flash today, and Nowa\'s AI agent is already running on it.","slug":"gemini-3-7-flash","date":"2026-08-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai"],"image":"/img/whats_new/Nowa-Gemini-3.7-Flash.png"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Design mode","permalink":"/new/whats-new/design-mode"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.10.5: Full mobile browser support","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-10-5"}},"content":"![Nowa\'s AI agent now runs on Gemini 3.7 Flash \u2014 smarter agent, double the limits](/img/whats_new/Nowa-Gemini-3.7-Flash.png)\\n\\nGoogle released **Gemini 3.7 Flash** today, and Nowa\'s AI agent is already running on it. \ud83d\ude80 The agent is noticeably better at building UIs, following a design, and finishing long multi-step tasks \u2014 and because the new model costs **50% less** than the one it replaces, we\'re passing that saving straight to you as **double the daily limits on every plan**, at the same price.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#gemini-37-flash-upgrade-13-august-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **Nowa AI now runs on Gemini 3.7 Flash**\\n  We switched the agent over the same day the model launched. What it means when you\'re building:\\n  - **Better screens on the first try** \u2014 3.7 Flash is currently ranked **#1 on Code Arena**, a public leaderboard where models go head-to-head on building real, working interfaces.\\n  - **Much better at following a design** \u2014 give it a screenshot, an image, or a design system and it sticks to it far more faithfully than before.\\n  - **It doesn\'t lose the thread on long tasks** \u2014 long, multi-step engineering work jumped from **49% to 65%** on the DeepSWE benchmark, so fewer retries and fewer moments where the agent forgets what you asked three steps ago.\\n  - **More correct code the first time** \u2014 production code quality went from **34.4% to 43.6%** on FrontierCode, which means less debugging for you.\\n\\n- \u26a1 **Double the daily limits, same price**\\n  The new model costs **half** of what the previous one did. Instead of keeping that saving, we doubled the daily limits on **every plan** \u2014 effective immediately, nothing to claim or upgrade. The new model is also more token-efficient, so it gets the same task done using fewer tokens: in day-to-day use it can feel like more than double. Any extra credits you buy now stretch across roughly twice the work too.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **Agent improvements, focused on UI generation**\\n  Alongside the model swap, we shipped a round of improvements to the agent itself with a particular focus on UI generation. Between our updates and the new model, this is the biggest single-day jump in quality the Nowa agent has ever had.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear what you build with the new agent! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-10-5","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-10-5","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-07-14-3-10-5.md","title":"Nowa 3.10.5: Full mobile browser support","description":"Nowa 3.10.5 brings the full Nowa experience to your phone! You can now open Nowa in your mobile browser to check projects, make quick updates, and even deploy while you\'re on the go.","date":"2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Account and teams","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/account","description":"Releases that changed your account, workspaces, organizations and the dashboard."},{"inline":false,"label":"Publish","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/publish","description":"Releases that changed deploying to the web and getting into the App Store and Google Play."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.10.5: Full mobile browser support","sidebar_label":"3.10.5 \xb7 Full mobile browser support","description":"Nowa 3.10.5 brings the full Nowa experience to your phone! You can now open Nowa in your mobile browser to check projects, make quick updates, and even deploy while you\'re on the go.","slug":"3-10-5","date":"2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["account","publish"],"image":"/img/whats_new/Nowa-3.10.5-Mobile.png"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Gemini 3.7 Flash upgrade","permalink":"/new/whats-new/gemini-3-7-flash"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.10: Local run for cloud projects","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-10"}},"content":"![Nowa 3.10.5 brings full mobile browser support](/img/whats_new/Nowa-3.10.5-Mobile.png)\\n\\nNowa 3.10.5 brings the full Nowa experience to your phone! \ud83d\udcf1 You can now open [Nowa](https://app.nowa.dev/) in your mobile browser to check projects, make quick updates, and even deploy while you\'re on the go. This release also improves workspaces, introduces a post-launch support package, and fixes Git issues on Windows.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3105-14-july-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udcf1 **Full Mobile Browser Support**\\n  Open Nowa directly from your smartphone and build smoothly from your mobile browser. Whether you\'re checking a project, making an update, or deploying your app, you can now do it from your pocket.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcc2 **Improved Workspace Experience**\\n  Workspaces are now easier to organize and manage, with improvements that help you:\\n  - Invite and collaborate with team members.\\n  - Organize your workspace.\\n  - Manage your projects more efficiently.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udf81 **Post-Launch Support Package**\\n  Successfully deployed an app with Nowa? You can now claim a special package directly from the **deployment panel** after launch. It includes:\\n  - **$25 in Nowa AI credits**.\\n  - Direct post-launch support from the Nowa team.\\n  - Help with gaining exposure, monetization, collecting feedback, and improving your app.\\n\\n## **What\'s Fixed \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f**\\n- \ud83e\ude9f **Git on Windows**\\n  Fixed an issue that affected some Windows users when working with Git in Nowa. Git should now work smoothly again.\\n\\n## **More Updates \ud83d\udce2**\\n- \ud83e\uddea **Nowa GO** \u2014 our dedicated Android and iOS app is still in private beta.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear what you think of building with Nowa from your phone! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-10","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-10","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-07-02-3-10.md","title":"Nowa 3.10: Local run for cloud projects","description":"Nowa 3.10 transforms how you test and deploy your apps. You can now run cloud projects directly on a local simulator or physical device \u2014 no cloning, no switching to local projects, with hot reload included.","date":"2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."},{"inline":false,"label":"Publish","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/publish","description":"Releases that changed deploying to the web and getting into the App Store and Google Play."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.10: Local run for cloud projects","sidebar_label":"3.10 \xb7 Local run for cloud projects","description":"Nowa 3.10 transforms how you test and deploy your apps. You can now run cloud projects directly on a local simulator or physical device \u2014 no cloning, no switching to local projects, with hot reload included.","slug":"3-10","date":"2026-07-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["preview","publish"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.10.5: Full mobile browser support","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-10-5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.9: A fully rebuilt AI system","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-9"}},"content":"Nowa 3.10 transforms how you test and deploy your apps. You can now run cloud projects directly on a **local simulator or physical device** \u2014 no cloning, no switching to local projects, with hot reload included. Combined with a brand-new **Run & Deploy UI** and major stability work, testing and shipping your apps has never been this simple.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udcf1 **Local Run for Cloud Projects**\\n  This is the big one! You no longer need to create a local project or clone your cloud project just to test on a simulator or physical device. Nowa now **generates temporary local files behind the scenes**, so any cloud project can run locally \u2014 and **hot reload works too**. Every change you make in Nowa shows up on your device instantly.\\n\\n- \ud83d\ude80 **New Run & Deploy UI**\\n  Every project now has **Run and Deploy buttons** in the top right, putting the whole flow in one place:\\n  - **Run** launches your app anywhere \u2014 inside Nowa, on a local simulator, or on your physical device.\\n  - **Deploy** ships your app to any platform, all from the same UI.\\n\\n- \u2601\ufe0f **Redesigned Deployment**\\n  All deployment options now live in one place. Once your setup is done, you can deploy to any platform from the main window with a **single click** \u2014 no more hunting through menus.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **A Cleaner Layout**\\n  Two refinements to give you more room to build:\\n  - **Boards moved to the top right**, making it easier to jump between boards and keeping the workspace cleaner.\\n  - **Toolbar moved to the bottom**, freeing up more space above for your work.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f **Major Stability Improvements**\\n  We\'ve done significant work under the hood across the entire platform, so everything should feel smoother and more reliable.\\n\\n## **More Updates \ud83d\udce2**\\n- \ud83d\ude4f **Thank you for the Free Weekend!** We loved seeing what you built \u2014 some of you created genuinely impressive apps that simply weren\'t possible before, and your feedback is already shaping what comes next. There are big things on the way. \ud83d\udd1c\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear what you think of Nowa 3.10! Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building as always!"},{"id":"3-9","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-9","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-06-13-3-9.md","title":"Nowa 3.9: A fully rebuilt AI system","description":"Nowa 3.9 is our most powerful release yet. It\'s the first version where building complex, top-tier apps with AI feels genuinely easy and efficient \u2014 powered by a fully rebuilt AI system and real in-app compiling with App Run.","date":"2026-06-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.9: A fully rebuilt AI system","sidebar_label":"3.9 \xb7 A fully rebuilt AI system","description":"Nowa 3.9 is our most powerful release yet. It\'s the first version where building complex, top-tier apps with AI feels genuinely easy and efficient \u2014 powered by a fully rebuilt AI system and real in-app compiling with App Run.","slug":"3-9","date":"2026-06-13T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","preview","design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.10: Local run for cloud projects","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-10"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.8.2: Nowa Run, a live preview of your real app","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-8-2"}},"content":"Nowa 3.9 is our most powerful release yet. \ud83d\ude80 It\'s the first version where building complex, top-tier apps with AI feels genuinely easy and efficient \u2014 powered by a **fully rebuilt AI system** and real in-app compiling with **App Run**. Together with a refreshed layout and a long list of improvements, this is where you can confidently build world-class apps, no matter the complexity, faster and easier than ever.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#39-13-june-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **A Fully Rebuilt AI System**\\n  We rebuilt our AI from the ground up into a **multi-agent system**, where several subagents work on your project in parallel \u2014 coordinating to plan, build, and refine your app at the same time. The result is **exceptional UI/UX** out of the box, **complex logic built reliably** even across large projects, smooth handling of **external pub.dev packages** (including any platform-file setup), and **smart context fetching** that reads exactly what\'s needed without over- or under-reading. Because it\'s so efficient, you get far more done **per credit** than ever before. This is the first version of our AI you can fully rely on for any use case.\\n\\n- \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f **Smarter Planning Mode**\\n  Planning mode now presents a clear, readable plan that anyone can follow \u2014 no technical skills required \u2014 and it\'s much better at matching what you actually want to build before any work begins.\\n\\n- \u25b6\ufe0f **App Run \u2014 Compile & Run Inside Nowa**\\n  You can now **compile and build your app directly inside Nowa**. When you play your app, Nowa compiles and runs it for real \u2014 exactly as it\'ll behave on deployment, including every pub.dev package, custom code block, and native part. In other words: what you see in App Run is what you\'ll ship.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfac **App Preview Is Back \u2014 Now on the Board**\\n  Many of you loved the instant play experience, so we brought it back and made it even more convenient. Just **hover over any screen on the board** and hit the play button to run your app right where you\'re working \u2014 no extra steps, no switching views.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **A Fresh, More Intuitive Layout**\\n  We reworked the interface to make building more enjoyable and easier to navigate:\\n  - **New Assets panel** for uploading and managing your assets.\\n  - **Outline moved to the left side**, giving you a cleaner workspace.\\n  - **A dedicated code editor** \u2014 click the `<>` icon in the top right to open the full code panel, and every change compiles automatically.\\n  - **Files merged into code editing** \u2014 the separate Files panel is gone; everything now lives in one place alongside your code.\\n  - **New deployment UI** with more detail and easier management.\\n  - **New settings page** \u2014 a cleaner, more organized home for your project settings.\\n  - **Smarter logs** that cover both App Run and preview, for full visibility into what\'s happening.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udf81 **Invite a Friend, Get 15 Credits Each**\\n  You can now **refer a friend** to Nowa. When they sign up, you both receive **15 free credits** \u2014 and with the new AI system, those credits go a long way.\\n\\n## **More Updates \ud83d\udce2**\\n- \ud83c\udd93 **Nowa Free Weekend** \u2014 this coming **Saturday and Sunday**, Nowa is **completely free** to use. If there\'s something you\'ve been waiting to build, now\'s the perfect time to dive in.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f We\'d love to hear what you think once you\'ve taken Nowa 3.9 for a spin \u2014 your feedback shapes where we go next. Click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`. Happy building!"},{"id":"3-8-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-8-2","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-06-04-3-8-2.md","title":"Nowa 3.8.2: Nowa Run, a live preview of your real app","description":"Nowa 3.8.2 brings something we\'ve wanted to ship for a long time: Nowa Run \u2014 a live, fully interactive preview of your real Flutter app, right inside your editor, updating as you build.","date":"2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.8.2: Nowa Run, a live preview of your real app","sidebar_label":"3.8.2 \xb7 Nowa Run, a live preview of your real app","description":"Nowa 3.8.2 brings something we\'ve wanted to ship for a long time: Nowa Run \u2014 a live, fully interactive preview of your real Flutter app, right inside your editor, updating as you build.","slug":"3-8-2","date":"2026-06-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["preview"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.9: A fully rebuilt AI system","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-9"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.8: Meet Nowa Agent 4","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-8"}},"content":"Nowa 3.8.2 brings something we\'ve wanted to ship for a long time: **Nowa Run** \u26a1 \u2014 a live, fully interactive preview of your real Flutter app, right inside your editor, updating as you build. No more picturing how your app will behave \u2014 just run it and watch. \ud83d\udc40\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83c\udfac **It\'s the Real App**\\n  Not a mockup or a rendered guess. **Tap, scroll, fill in forms, and test your logic** \u2014 it behaves exactly like your shipped app, because it *is* the app.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udce6 **Packages Actually Work**\\n  Third-party packages now **run for real instead of being mocked**, so you see their true behavior right in the preview.\\n\\n- \u26a1 **Edits Show Up in Seconds**\\n  Change something in the builder and the preview updates **almost instantly** \u2014 no manual refresh.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcf1 **Preview on Your Phone**\\n  Open the preview on your **actual device** and watch it update live as you make changes in Nowa. Build on your screen, see it on your phone.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd04 **Resilient**\\n  If a preview ever hits a snag, just **restart it and keep going** in the same session \u2014 never starting from scratch.\\n\\nThis is a big step toward making Nowa feel less like building blind and more like **building with your app in the room**. More on the way to make the loop even tighter. \ud83d\udd1c\\n\\n## **What\'s Fixed \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f**\\n- \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f Fixed a bug where the editor would sometimes show **\\"file not found\\"** when compiling changes.\\n- \ud83c\udf10 Removed the **Development environment** for Web Preview/Deploy, as Nowa Run covers its use cases more efficiently.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f Built something in Nowa you\'re proud of? Show us \u2014 we love seeing what you make! Or click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-8","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-8","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-06-02-3-8.md","title":"Nowa 3.8: Meet Nowa Agent 4","description":"Nowa 3.8 is here, and it\'s a big one! Say hello to Nowa Agent 4, our best AI agent ever. It runs multiple agents in parallel to take on longer, more complex tasks, consumes fewer credits, and now drops your new screens onto the board automatically.","date":"2026-06-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.8: Meet Nowa Agent 4","sidebar_label":"3.8 \xb7 Meet Nowa Agent 4","description":"Nowa 3.8 is here, and it\'s a big one! Say hello to Nowa Agent 4, our best AI agent ever. It runs multiple agents in parallel to take on longer, more complex tasks, consumes fewer credits, and now drops your new screens onto the board automatically.","slug":"3-8","date":"2026-06-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.8.2: Nowa Run, a live preview of your real app","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-8-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.7.3: Localisation support","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7-3"}},"content":"Nowa 3.8 is here, and it\'s a big one! \ud83d\ude80 Say hello to **Nowa Agent 4**, our best AI agent ever. It runs **multiple agents in parallel** to take on longer, more complex tasks, **consumes fewer credits**, and now drops your **new screens onto the board automatically**.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Meet Nowa Agent 4**\\n  Our brand new AI agent works very differently from the previous ones. Instead of one agent doing everything, it can now run **multiple agents in parallel** on your project at once. That means it can take on longer, more complex tasks and still stay precise, while you keep full visual control.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udfaf **Better Results**\\n  Agent 4 does noticeably better on things like **multi-screen generation, complex bug fixing, advanced designs, and tricky logic**. It can work for longer and split the work across subagents to get there.\\n\\n- \ud83e\ude99 **Fewer Credits**\\n  It now handles **reading and writing with separate agents** instead of one. That makes it more efficient and brings your costs down.\\n\\n- \u2699\ufe0f **Works with Platform Files**\\n  Agent 4 can now touch **platform files**, not just Dart files. So it can **set permissions, manage packages, and more** \u2014 and you don\'t have to do that by hand anymore.\\n\\n- \u26a1 **Faster \\"Instant\\" Tasks**\\n  Instant is now up to **5x faster**, and uses at least **2x fewer credits** than before.\\n\\n- \u2705 **See What the AI Did, Right Away**\\n  New screens **show up on your board automatically** as Agent 4 adds them \u2014 no more dragging and dropping. \ud83d\udc40\\n\\n> \u26a0\ufe0f **Heads up:** You might lose access to your previous AI conversation history with this update. We recommend **starting a new chat**. If you need to fetch a previous history, just let us know.\\n\\n## **What\'s Coming Next \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f We\'ve got **another big Nowa update** in the works to make building even smoother. More on that soon! \ud83d\udd1c\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you\'ve built something in Nowa and want us to take a look, just let us know \u2014 we\'d love to see it! Or click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-7-3","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7-3","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-04-26-3-7-3.md","title":"Nowa 3.7.3: Localisation support","description":"Nowa 3.7.3 brings localisation support, AI font downloads, and smarter package conflict handling \u2014 making it easier to ship apps in multiple languages and match designs pixel-perfect.","date":"2026-04-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.7.3: Localisation support","sidebar_label":"3.7.3 \xb7 Localisation support","description":"Nowa 3.7.3 brings localisation support, AI font downloads, and smarter package conflict handling \u2014 making it easier to ship apps in multiple languages and match designs pixel-perfect.","slug":"3-7-3","date":"2026-04-26T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.8: Meet Nowa Agent 4","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-8"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.7.2: A new packaging system","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7-2"}},"content":"Nowa 3.7.3 brings **localisation support**, **AI font downloads**, and **smarter package conflict handling** \u2014 making it easier to ship apps in multiple languages and match designs pixel-perfect.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#373-26-april-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83c\udf0d **Localisation Support**\\n  You asked, we delivered! You can now make your app run in **multiple languages** with ease. Just ask Nowa AI to set it up and it\'ll handle everything for you, end to end.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd24 **AI Can Now Download Fonts**\\n  Ask Nowa AI to set any font you want, and if it\'s not already in your project, it\'ll **download and set it up automatically**. Super handy when you\'re importing designs from Figma or other tools and want Nowa AI to match them pixel-perfect.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udce6 **Smarter Package Conflict Handling**\\n  Another upgrade to our packaging system! If packages are clashing, Nowa AI now **detects and resolves the conflict automatically**, so you can stay focused on the big picture instead of digging through dependency errors.\\n\\n## **More Updates \ud83d\udce2**\\n- \ud83d\udcf1 **Nowa GO is already rolling out in batches!** If you haven\'t signed up yet and want to give it a shot, now\'s the time. Build on your phone or tablet, anywhere you go.\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you face any issue, click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-7-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7-2","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-04-23-3-7-2.md","title":"Nowa 3.7.2: A new packaging system","description":"Nowa 3.7.2 is a big step forward \u2014 packages are now way more stable, the experimental UI is getting closer to a whole new way of building, and we solved some important issues along the way.","date":"2026-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.7.2: A new packaging system","sidebar_label":"3.7.2 \xb7 A new packaging system","description":"Nowa 3.7.2 is a big step forward \u2014 packages are now way more stable, the experimental UI is getting closer to a whole new way of building, and we solved some important issues along the way.","slug":"3-7-2","date":"2026-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["code","nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.7.3: Localisation support","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7-3"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.7: Stripe payments","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7"}},"content":"Nowa 3.7.2 is a big step forward \u2014 **packages are now way more stable**, the **experimental UI** is getting closer to a whole new way of building, and we solved some important issues along the way.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#372-23-april-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udce6 **New Packaging System**\\n  We\'ve massively improved how Nowa integrates with **pub.dev packages**. It\'s way more stable now, and Nowa AI handles external packages much better than before. Bonus: projects now load faster since packages load *after* the project opens \u26a1\\n\\n- \ud83e\uddea **Experimental UI Updates**\\n  Big changes landed here. AI has moved to a **toolbar at the bottom of the board** \u2014 just hit **/** to start chatting, while seeing your project components in real-time on the side. This is a step toward a completely new experience that\'ll make building faster and easier. Enable it from **App Settings \u2192 Project details \u2192 Experimentals**, then turn on **\\"New UX\\"** \ud83d\ude80\\n\\n## **What\'s Fixed \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f**\\n- \ud83d\udd17 **Missing imports** \u2014 AI can now work with imports properly, resolving issues some of you ran into on certain projects.\\n- \ud83c\udf9e\ufe0f **Rive widget on Web** \u2014 Fixed.\\n- \ud83c\udf10 **AI + APIs** \u2014 We noticed some of you hit walls when asking AI to integrate APIs. That\'s sorted now.\\n\\n## **What\'s Coming Next \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **A new AI system** that delivers much better results while cutting credit costs by **5\u201315x**\\n- \ud83d\ude80 **A major deployment upgrade**, making deployments easier and clearer than ever\\n- \ud83c\udfa8 **More experimental UI updates** on the way"},{"id":"3-7","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-04-12-3-7.md","title":"Nowa 3.7: Stripe payments","description":"Nowa 3.7 makes it easier than ever to build, monetize, and maintain your apps. This release brings Stripe payments, in-app support chat, in-app notifications, AI-powered project fixing, and a preview of Nowa\'s redesigned UI.","date":"2026-04-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.7: Stripe payments","sidebar_label":"3.7 \xb7 Stripe payments","description":"Nowa 3.7 makes it easier than ever to build, monetize, and maintain your apps. This release brings Stripe payments, in-app support chat, in-app notifications, AI-powered project fixing, and a preview of Nowa\'s redesigned UI.","slug":"3-7","date":"2026-04-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations","nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.7.2: A new packaging system","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.6.1: A fully editable main.dart","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-6-1"}},"content":"Nowa 3.7 makes it easier than ever to build, monetize, and maintain your apps. This release brings **Stripe payments**, **in-app support chat**, **in-app notifications**, **AI-powered project fixing**, and a **preview of Nowa\'s redesigned UI**.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udcb3 **Stripe Payments Integration**\\n  Want to monetize your app? Now you can! **Stripe is fully integrated** \u2014 whether it\'s subscriptions or one-time payments, Nowa sets everything up for you, including webhooks. You focus on your app, we handle the plumbing.\\n  Watch the tutorial here: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8QjTKvSBTdM\\n\\n- \ud83d\udcac **In-App Support Chat**\\n  Building should never feel lonely. Click the **? icon** in the bottom-right corner to **chat with us directly** \u2014 ask questions, report issues, attach your project, and follow your report status from submitted all the way to done.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd14 **In-App Notifications**\\n  New tutorials, updates, and tips \u2014 we\'ll now **notify you right inside Nowa** so you always have what you need to level up your apps.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **AI Project Fixer**\\n  Bugs slowing you down? Just say **\\"Fix problems in my project\\"** and let the AI do a full scan and fix issues before you deploy. Smoother builds, fewer headaches.\\n\\n- \u2728 **Redesigned UI (Preview)**\\n  We\'re redesigning Nowa from the ground up to make building even more intuitive. Curious? Turn it on in **Settings \u2192 Experiments** and tell us what you think!\\n\\n## **More Updates \ud83d\udce2**\\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **New tutorial** \u2014 Watch us build a [full CRM app for VCs](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IWlPbIRTE9Y&t=1528) from scratch\\n- \ud83d\udcf1 **Nowa GO is almost here** \u2014 build on your phone or tablet, anywhere you go\\n- \ud83d\udcb0 **Earn with Nowa** \u2014 Content creators can earn commissions through **Nowa Creators**. Reach out at `team@nowa.dev`\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you face any issue, click the **? icon** to chat with us directly, or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-6-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-6-1","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-03-12-3-6-1.md","title":"Nowa 3.6.1: A fully editable main.dart","description":"A hotfix following 3.6 that makes main.dart fully editable \u2014 a new system now lets both you and the AI agent freely modify the main.dart file without running into issues.","date":"2026-03-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.6.1: A fully editable main.dart","sidebar_label":"3.6.1 \xb7 A fully editable main.dart","description":"A hotfix following 3.6 that makes main.dart fully editable \u2014 a new system now lets both you and the AI agent freely modify the main.dart file without running into issues.","slug":"3-6-1","date":"2026-03-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.7: Stripe payments","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-7"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.6: In-app purchases with RevenueCat","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-6"}},"content":"A hotfix following 3.6 that makes `main.dart` fully editable \u2014 a new system now lets both you and the AI agent freely modify the `main.dart` file without running into issues.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#361-12-march-2026).\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you face any issue, use the **\\"Problem\\"** button to report it (attach a project snapshot if needed), or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-6","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-6","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-03-06-3-6.md","title":"Nowa 3.6: In-app purchases with RevenueCat","description":"Nowa 3.6 brings a big boost to what you can do. Now you can offer in-app purchases with RevenueCat, use Planning Mode to get much more accurate results from AI, get solid results for complex prompts in Agent Mode, and more improvements to make your day-to-day building smoother.","date":"2026-03-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.6: In-app purchases with RevenueCat","sidebar_label":"3.6 \xb7 In-app purchases with RevenueCat","description":"Nowa 3.6 brings a big boost to what you can do. Now you can offer in-app purchases with RevenueCat, use Planning Mode to get much more accurate results from AI, get solid results for complex prompts in Agent Mode, and more improvements to make your day-to-day building smoother.","slug":"3-6","date":"2026-03-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations","nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.6.1: A fully editable main.dart","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-6-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.5: Nowa Agent V3","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-5"}},"content":"Nowa 3.6 brings a big boost to what you can do. Now you can offer **in-app purchases with RevenueCat**, use **Planning Mode** to get much more accurate results from AI, get solid results for complex prompts in **Agent Mode**, and more improvements to make your day-to-day building smoother.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nWant to see everything in action? Watch the Dev Diary:\\n  <iframe width=\\"767\\" height=\\"431\\" src=\\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/dLsO05crdSk\\" title=\\"Nowa 3.6 | Dev Diary\\" frameborder=\\"0\\" allow=\\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\\" referrerpolicy=\\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#36-6-march-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udcb0 **In-App Purchases with RevenueCat**\\n  You can now add in-app purchases to your iOS and Android apps with just a few clicks through **RevenueCat**. If you\'ve been wanting to monetize your app, this is the easiest way to get started. A step-by-step tutorial is coming in the next few days.\\n\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **AI Planning Mode**\\n  Instead of jumping straight into implementation, **Planning Mode** takes the time to understand what you\'re trying to build, analyzes your project in depth, asks you the right questions, and lays out a clear plan for you to review before anything gets implemented.\\n  You can keep refining the plan until you\'re happy with it, then let it build \u2014 so you get what you actually wanted without the back and forth.\\n\\n- \u2705 **Todos in Agent Mode**\\n  For complex requests and long prompts, the agent now creates its own **internal todo list** and works through tasks one by one, allowing it to stay focused and produce much better results along the way.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd0d **Smarter Search**\\n  The AI agent is now much more efficient at searching across your project, making your prompts **faster** and **lighter on credits**.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd2c **Source-Code Analysis**\\n  The agent can now trigger **deep analysis** directly on the source code to catch problems there, making it way more reliable at debugging and able to detect all kinds of issues.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udccb **Automatic Issue Reporting**\\n  If the AI runs into something unexpected, it reports it directly to us and shares a **report ID** with you to follow up. No personal data is collected \u2014 this just helps us support you better if something happens.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd10 **Google Sign-In with Supabase**\\n  You can now implement Google Sign-In using Supabase easily. Just connect your project to Supabase and ask Nowa AI to set it up for you.\\n\\n- \ud83c\udf93 **Onboarding for New Projects**\\n  Starting a new project? You\'ll now get a guided **onboarding experience** to help you get up and running quickly.\\n\\n## **Community Highlights \ud83c\udf1f**\\n- \ud83c\uddf8\ud83c\uddea **[Klubbrabatten](https://klubbrabatten.se/)** \u2014 Sweden\'s biggest loyalty rewards program, giving users discounts across restaurants and places all over the country. Used by over **150,000 users** and built entirely with Nowa and Supabase.\\n- \ud83c\udfcb\ufe0f **[Zero-Trust Fitness App](https://github.com/EdoSag/Zero-Trust-Fitness)** \u2014 an open-source, privacy-first alternative to Google Fit that encrypts all your health data, built by **Edo**. Want to contribute? Clone the project and jump in!\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you face any issue, use the **\\"Problem\\"** button to report it (attach a project snapshot if needed), or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-5","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-5","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-02-09-3-5.md","title":"Nowa 3.5: Nowa Agent V3","description":"Nowa 3.5 is a big step forward. In this release, you\u2019ll get Nowa Agent V3 (a new AI foundation), a new routing system powered by GoRouter, Git support for Local Projects, and smoother performance across the editor.","date":"2026-02-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.5: Nowa Agent V3","sidebar_label":"3.5 \xb7 Nowa Agent V3","description":"Nowa 3.5 is a big step forward. In this release, you\u2019ll get Nowa Agent V3 (a new AI foundation), a new routing system powered by GoRouter, Git support for Local Projects, and smoother performance across the editor.","slug":"3-5","date":"2026-02-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","logic","code","design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.6: In-app purchases with RevenueCat","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-6"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.4: Supabase MCP","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-4"}},"content":"Nowa 3.5 is a big step forward. In this release, you\u2019ll get **Nowa Agent V3** (a new AI foundation), a new routing system powered by **GoRouter**, **Git support for Local Projects**, and smoother performance across the editor.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#35-9-february-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udd16 **Nowa Agent V3 (4 modes)**  \\n  This is the biggest change in 3.5 \u2014 we rebuilt how AI works in Nowa.  \\n\\n  You now have four modes to choose from: **Instant, Thinking, Deep Thinking, and Max**. The new modes (except Max) consume **5\xd7 fewer credits**, run **4\xd7 faster**, and produce **2\u20133\xd7 better results**.  \\n\\n  In practice, you\u2019ll notice:  \\n  - Better UI/UX generated out of the box  \\n  - Stronger Supabase workflows using **Supabase MCP** (including more complex cases)  \\n  - Better planning and debugging for bigger tasks  \\n  - Deeper understanding of Nowa projects and newer Flutter capabilities  \\n\\n- \ud83e\udded **Routing is now GoRouter by default**  \\n  All new projects now use **GoRouter**. Each screen has a **path**, so your web apps can navigate with real links and URLs, and your mobile apps can support **deep linking** (for example from notifications).  \\n  It also makes building navigation patterns like **Navigation Bars** and **Drawers** much simpler and cleaner.  \\n\\n- \ud83c\udf3f **Git for Local Projects**  \\n  Local projects now come with **Git enabled by default**, so you can track changes, discard them when needed, commit your work, review history, and push to GitHub (or any Git provider) \u2014 just like a real production workflow.  \\n\\n- \u26a1 **Smoother UI boards**  \\n  We improved how boards are rendered \u2014 moving between screens, panning, and zooming should feel **significantly smoother**, even when your board has many screens.  \\n\\n## **New Content \ud83d\udcda**\\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **Dev Diary (Nowa 3.5)**  \\n  Want to see everything in action? Watch here:  \\n  <iframe width=\\"767\\" height=\\"431\\" src=\\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/CuR6uC32ulE\\" title=\\"Nowa 3.5 | Introducing Nowa AI Agent V3 | Dev Diary\\" frameborder=\\"0\\" allow=\\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\\" referrerpolicy=\\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\\" allowfullscreen></iframe>  \\n\\n## **Community Reward \ud83c\udf81**\\n- \ud83c\udf81 **Get 50 free AI credits**  \\n  Share a **complete app** you built and deployed with Nowa on **LinkedIn or X**, tag us, and you\u2019ll get **50 free AI credits**.  \\n  The **top 5 apps** shared will get **1 month free on the Scale plan** (and if you\u2019re already on Scale, you\u2019ll get a refund for that month).  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you face any issue, use the **\\"Problem\\"** button to report it (attach a project snapshot if needed), or email us at `team@nowa.dev`."},{"id":"3-4","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-4","source":"@site/whats-new/2026-01-19-3-4.md","title":"Nowa 3.4: Supabase MCP","description":"This is one of our biggest releases yet \u2014 introducing Supabase MCP and a new Agent Creation Summary for faster, clearer AI workflows.","date":"2026-01-19T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.4: Supabase MCP","sidebar_label":"3.4 \xb7 Supabase MCP","description":"This is one of our biggest releases yet \u2014 introducing Supabase MCP and a new Agent Creation Summary for faster, clearer AI workflows.","slug":"3-4","date":"2026-01-19T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","integrations"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.5: Nowa Agent V3","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.3.5: Commit history in Nowa","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-3-5"}},"content":"This is one of our biggest releases yet \u2014 introducing **Supabase MCP** and a new **Agent Creation Summary** for faster, clearer AI workflows.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#34-19-january-2026).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **Supabase MCP (Frontend + Backend from one panel)**  \\n  From now on, building a serious full stack app has never been easier! With Supabase MCP, Nowa agent can manage your full backend besides the frontend, allowing you to build the app you want with way less effort.\\n\\n  Connect your Supabase project and let the AI Agent set up everything end\u2011to\u2011end such as:  \\n  - Create tables and database structure  \\n  - Generate RLS policies  \\n  - Set up triggers and Edge Functions  \\n\\n  To use it, enable Supabase MCP it in the agent chat, then describe what you want and let the agent do the full work for you!  \\n\\n- \ud83d\udccb **Agent Creation Summary**  \\n  After each AI chat, you\u2019ll now see a summary box showing **everything the agent created**.  \\n  - Drag and drop items to the board  \\n  - Click any item to preview it in the file viewer  \\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **New Tutorials**  \\nWe have released the following new tutorials on YouTube:\\n  - Google Maps integration: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1aqqNMtRKQU  \\n  - Instant preview sharing (testing & feedback): https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ORa4ohpK4pQ"},{"id":"3-3-5","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-3-5","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-12-30-3-3-5.md","title":"Nowa 3.3.5: Commit history in Nowa","description":"Say hi to Commit History, one\u2011click GitHub integration, and faster loading for local projects.","date":"2025-12-30T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.3.5: Commit history in Nowa","sidebar_label":"3.3.5 \xb7 Commit history in Nowa","description":"Say hi to Commit History, one\u2011click GitHub integration, and faster loading for local projects.","slug":"3-3-5","date":"2025-12-30T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.4: Supabase MCP","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.3.2: Google Maps in Nowa","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-3-2"}},"content":"Say hi to **Commit History, one\u2011click GitHub integration, and faster loading for local projects**. Let\'s get into details:\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#335-30-december-2025).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udd52 **Commit History in Nowa**  \\n  You can now browse your **full commit history directly inside the Git panel** without needing GitHub.  \\n  - Preview all previous commits and see which files were created, modified, or removed  \\n  - Click any file to inspect **line\u2011by\u2011line changes**  \\n  - Right\u2011click a commit and choose **\u201cRevert\u201d** to roll back its changes  \\n  > Note: Commit History is currently available for **Cloud projects**. For Local projects, you can continue using GitHub Desktop, other IDEs, or the command line.  \\n\\n- \ud83d\udc19 **One\u2011click GitHub Integration**  \\n  Connecting your project to GitHub is now a **single click** away \u2014 no manual tokens required.  \\n  - Go to `Project Settings \u2192 Git \u2192 Connect to GitHub`  \\n  - Authenticate Nowa in the window that opens  \\n  - Return to Nowa and you\u2019re connected, ready to push and pull from your repository  \\n\\n- \ud83d\udcbd **Faster Loading for Local Projects**  \\n  Local projects with lots of dependencies now **load much faster**.  \\n  - Nowa 3.3.5 uses your **local Flutter SDK** to resolve dependencies  \\n  - This removes the need to fetch them all again from `pub.dev`, especially for large projects"},{"id":"3-3-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-3-2","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-12-10-3-3-2.md","title":"Nowa 3.3.2: Google Maps in Nowa","description":"Say hello to Google Maps in Nowa! This update brings new power to your apps with built-in Maps support, along with smoother performance across the board.","date":"2025-12-10T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.3.2: Google Maps in Nowa","sidebar_label":"3.3.2 \xb7 Google Maps in Nowa","description":"Say hello to Google Maps in Nowa! This update brings new power to your apps with built-in Maps support, along with smoother performance across the board.","slug":"3-3-2","date":"2025-12-10T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.3.5: Commit history in Nowa","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-3-5"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.2: AI that uses custom packages","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-2"}},"content":"Say hello to **Google Maps in Nowa!** This update brings new power to your apps with built-in Maps support, along with smoother performance across the board.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#332-10-december-2025).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f **Google Maps Widget**  \\n  You can now add and customize **Google Maps** directly inside Nowa \u2014 no need for custom code!  \\n  - Add from the **Widget Picker**  \\n  - Configure it visually or through AI  \\n  - Run it in the simulator to view live map results  \\n\\n## **Improved Experience \u26a1**  \\n- Better loading visuals when opening projects for more transparency.  \\n- More consistent UI rendering when switching between screens and views.  \\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83e\udde9 **Supabase & Figma MCPs:** Connect your backend and design directly into Nowa.  \\n- \u2699\ufe0f **AI Upgrade:** Faster, smarter, and more context-aware AI generation.  \\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **New Video Series:** Full onboarding and crash course for new users."},{"id":"3-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-2","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-11-14-3-2.md","title":"Nowa 3.2: AI that uses custom packages","description":"This update makes Nowa\u2019s AI smarter, more capable, and fully connected to the Flutter ecosystem \u2014 introducing AI that can use custom packages from pub.dev!","date":"2025-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.2: AI that uses custom packages","sidebar_label":"3.2 \xb7 AI that uses custom packages","description":"This update makes Nowa\u2019s AI smarter, more capable, and fully connected to the Flutter ecosystem \u2014 introducing AI that can use custom packages from pub.dev!","slug":"3-2","date":"2025-11-14T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.3.2: Google Maps in Nowa","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-3-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.1.2: Improved AI stability","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-1-2"}},"content":"This update makes Nowa\u2019s AI **smarter, more capable, and fully connected to the Flutter ecosystem** \u2014 introducing **AI that can use custom packages from pub.dev!**  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#320-14-november-2025).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **AI That Uses Custom Packages**  \\n  The AI can now **fetch and use packages directly from pub.dev**, reading their docs, understanding their APIs, and implementing them automatically in your project \u2014 even if they aren\u2019t built into Nowa.  \\n  > \u2699\ufe0f Enabled by default for new projects  \\n  > \ud83e\uddea For existing ones: Go to `Settings \u2192 Packages \u2192 Enable \u201cLoad Packages (Experimental)\u201d`  \\n\\n- \u26a1 **Smarter, Cleaner AI**  \\n  The AI now fully understands Flutter\u2019s **Material library** and core widgets \u2014 meaning no more \u201cundefined\u201d issues and more precise results.  \\n  It also uses **new internal tools** to build cleaner architectures, connect logic and UI automatically, and follow your themes naturally.  \\n\\n- \ud83c\udf10 **Built-in Cloud Git Integration**  \\n  Every **cloud project** now comes with **Git pre-configured**.  \\n  You\u2019ll see visual indicators for pending changes and can commit directly within Nowa to keep your project\u2019s version history clean and easy to manage.  \\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83e\udde9 **Supabase & Figma MCPs:** Build your frontend, backend, and UI all from Nowa AI.  \\n- \u2699\ufe0f **AI Core Boost:** Improving reasoning, context awareness, and result accuracy.  \\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **Nowa Onboarding Video:** Learn the platform in under 15 minutes."},{"id":"3-1-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-1-2","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-10-25-3-1-2.md","title":"Nowa 3.1.2: Improved AI stability","description":"A quick update following the 3.1 release, improving the AI agent experience and reliability to make working with it smoother and more stable.","date":"2025-10-25T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.1.2: Improved AI stability","sidebar_label":"3.1.2 \xb7 Improved AI stability","description":"A quick update following the 3.1 release, improving the AI agent experience and reliability to make working with it smoother and more stable.","slug":"3-1-2","date":"2025-10-25T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","preview"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.2: AI that uses custom packages","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.1: A new AI system","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-1"}},"content":"A quick update following the 3.1 release, improving the **AI agent experience and reliability** to make working with it smoother and more stable.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#312-25-october-2025).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **Improved AI Stability**  \\n  The AI now handles larger prompts, streams responses more reliably, and maintains more consistent performance in long chats.  \\n\\n- \ud83d\udd17 **Better Sharing Experience**  \\n  Shared links and public previews now open instantly without login issues.  \\n\\n- \u2699\ufe0f **Improved Bug Reporting Flow**  \\n  You can now include more context automatically when submitting issues, helping the team fix things faster.  \\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **AI Quick Guide:** Short video on how to use the new AI agent.  \\n- \ud83d\ude80 **Onboarding Walkthrough:** Learn everything new in Nowa 3.1 in minutes."},{"id":"3-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-1","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-10-21-3-1.md","title":"Nowa 3.1: A new AI system","description":"This is our biggest update since V3.0 - with a brand\u2011new AI agent, Cloud Local Sync, Instant Sharing, and major performance upgrades.","date":"2025-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.1: A new AI system","sidebar_label":"3.1 \xb7 A new AI system","description":"This is our biggest update since V3.0 - with a brand\u2011new AI agent, Cloud Local Sync, Instant Sharing, and major performance upgrades.","slug":"3-1","date":"2025-10-21T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","code","preview"],"image":"/img/whats_new/nowa3_1.png"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.1.2: Improved AI stability","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-1-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.10: Notifications and Supabase Storage","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-10"}},"content":"This is our biggest update since V3.0 - with a brand\u2011new AI agent, Cloud Local Sync, Instant Sharing, and major performance upgrades.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n![](/img/whats_new/nowa3_1.png)\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#310-21-october-2025).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83e\udde0 **New AI System**  \\n  Rebuilt from the ground up for speed, stability, and much better results.  \\n  - The new agent is simply \u26a1 4\xd7 faster with 3\xd7 better results than the previous one   \\n  - \ud83d\udcac Stream Mode: You can see the results now live in real time  \\n  - \ud83d\udd27 The Agent checks for it\'s results and fix them on the spot with the same prompt   \\n  - \u2753 It Asks clarifying questions when it\'s unsure instead of making assumptions, leading to results that are more of what you expect.  \\n  - \ud83c\udfae It can run the app automatically to test and catch runtime issues and fix them  \\n  - \ud83d\uddc2 You have now Chat history saved per project to resume any previous conversation with its full context  \\n  - \ud83c\udfaf We changed the usage tracking from per-prompt to a wew credit system that relies fully on tokens for more fair use. (e.g., ~0.1 credit for redesigning a card components, ~1 credit for generating a full funtional screen). You can see the credit consumption for each prompt and for the overall chat as well. In settings you will see a history for your AI consumption.\\n\\n- \u2601\ufe0f **Cloud + Local Sync**  \\n  No need to choose if your project should be a local or cloud one. The same project can live on both now, with you being able to sync them with a click (no Git needed). \\n  Simply inside your project, click on the `Settings` icon -> `Project Sync`, and there you will be able to sync a cloud project to local or vise versa.\\n\\n- \ud83d\udd17 **Instant Preview Sharing**  \\n  You can now share the instant preview that you use inside Nowa with others! Simply click on the share button on the toolbar inside Nowa to share the instant preview privatly (with people in your workspace) or publicly with anyone.\\n  They will be able to view the app as well insantly without building.\\n  Compare to deploying to Web, this allows you to share without even the need for hosting for faster sharing from your side and faster viewing from the other side.\\n\\n## **New Content \ud83d\udcda**\\n- \ud83d\udcd8 **New Docs:**  at [docs.nowa.dev](https://docs.nowa.dev)  \\n- \ud83c\udf1f **Showcase Page:** at [nowa.dev/showcase](https://nowa.dev/showcase) \\n- \ud83c\udfe2 **Nowa Agency:** You can make our team build your full app and handle it in Nowa. 50% cheaper and 3x fastet than other agemncies. [Apply here](https://forms.gle/2VbmrP3tUMfkrGjP8)\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83e\udde9 You will be able to any package from pub.dev directly in Nowa without even using custom code  \\n- \ud83d\udce5 Importer V2: You will be able to import any Flutter project even the ones built outside Nowa  \\n- \ud83e\udde0 AI Planning Mode: the AI agent will be able to make a dynamic plan for complex prompts for better results when it comes to app-level prompts.  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f Please keep using the in\u2011app Feedback button to report issues or share ideas \u2014 it helps us make Nowa better much faster :)"},{"id":"3-0-10","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-10","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-10-07-3-0-10.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.10: Notifications and Supabase Storage","description":"We excited to introduce two powerful new features \u2014 Notifications and Supabase Storage \u2014 plus a brand-new syncing system between Nowa and your code files, that makes building smoother than ever.","date":"2025-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.10: Notifications and Supabase Storage","sidebar_label":"3.0.10 \xb7 Notifications and Supabase Storage","description":"We excited to introduce two powerful new features \u2014 Notifications and Supabase Storage \u2014 plus a brand-new syncing system between Nowa and your code files, that makes building smoother than ever.","slug":"3-0-10","date":"2025-10-07T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations","code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.1: A new AI system","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.9: Reliability fixes","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-9"}},"content":"We excited to introduce two powerful new features \u2014 **Notifications** and **Supabase Storage** \u2014 plus a brand-new syncing system between Nowa and your code files, that makes building smoother than ever.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#3010-7-october-2025).\\n\\n## **New in This Version \u2728**\\n- \ud83d\udd14 **Firebase Notifications:**  \\n  You can now offer **real-time notifications** in your app with few clicks! Once you connect your project to Firebase, you can send messages from the Firebase panel, from Nowa, or even through APIs like Supabase Cloud Functions. Enable it from Firebase settings in your project.\\n\\n- \u2601\ufe0f **Supabase Storage:**  \\n  You can now **store and retrieve files** from Supabase Storage \u2014 this, along side using Supabase Auth and tables in your app, makes it possible to build a full functional apps where data and assets are binded to specific users.  \\n\\n- \ud83d\udd04 **Smarter Code Sync:**  \\n  The new sync system makes working with code feel seamless.  \\n  Every change updates instantly in your UI without the board refreshing or repositioning for items, make it feel super natual to work with code files alongside Nowa  \\n\\n## **Content \ud83d\udcda**\\n- \ud83d\udcd8 **Docs for Nowa 3.0 are Live!**  \\n  The documentation has been fully updated to focus on Nowa 3.0, with also new sections regarding using Nowa AI, APIs, Supabase, local projects, and more.  \\n  \ud83d\udc49 Explore it here: [docs.nowa.dev](https://docs.nowa.dev)  \\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **New Tutorial:**  \\n  Learn how to build a beautiful **Movie App** using Nowa and APIs \u2014 [Watch Part 1](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=COpngAiqm0o). You can try the app yourself here\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd2e**\\n- \ud83d\ude80 **Nowa 3.1:** Our biggest update since 3.0 \u2014 featuring a more stable AI, restore points, chat history, a token-based credit system, and instant Cloud + Local sync.  \\n- \ud83c\udf1f **Showcase Page:** Discover real apps built with Nowa, complete with live demos.  \\n- \ud83c\udfe2 **Agency Program:** Special deals and support for development agencies \u2014 reach out to `team@nowa.dev` to know more!  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you encounter any issues, please report them using the **in-app Feedback** button \u2014 it helps us improve it for you pretty fast."},{"id":"3-0-9","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-9","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-09-19-3-0-9.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.9: Reliability fixes","description":"Nowa 3.0.9 is a small but important update focused on fixing some issues that improve reliability and usability.","date":"2025-09-19T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.9: Reliability fixes","sidebar_label":"3.0.9 \xb7 Reliability fixes","description":"Nowa 3.0.9 is a small but important update focused on fixing some issues that improve reliability and usability.","slug":"3-0-9","date":"2025-09-19T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.10: Notifications and Supabase Storage","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-10"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.8: New templates","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-8"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0.9 is a small but important update focused on **fixing some issues** that improve reliability and usability.  \\nCheck all fixes in the [ChangeLog](/new/change-log#309-19-september-2025)."},{"id":"3-0-8","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-8","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-09-17-3-0-8.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.8: New templates","description":"Nowa 3.0.8 introduces new templates, workflow improvements, and key fixes to make your building experience smoother and more reliable.","date":"2025-09-17T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.8: New templates","sidebar_label":"3.0.8 \xb7 New templates","description":"Nowa 3.0.8 introduces new templates, workflow improvements, and key fixes to make your building experience smoother and more reliable.","slug":"3-0-8","date":"2025-09-17T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.9: Reliability fixes","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-9"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.6: Stability fixes","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-6"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0.8 introduces **new templates, workflow improvements, and key fixes** to make your building experience smoother and more reliable.  \\nCheck all details in the [ChangeLog](/new/change-log#308-17-september-2025).  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **Fixes & Improvements \ud83d\udee0**  \\n- \ud83e\udde9 Added **new stunning templates** that match the quality of Nowa 3.0 \u2014 replacing the old ones with fresh, modern designs.  \\n- \ud83c\udfa8 Removed the older way of changing themes to simplify the workflow.  \\n- \u26a0\ufe0f Error build design is now clearer and clickable, so you can quickly access build logs when needed.  \\n- \ud83d\udcd1 Added the option to **include cloud build logs** when submitting bug reports \u2014 making issue reporting faster and debugging easier.  \\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n- \ud83e\udd16 A **new AI system** that feels smoother, produces better results, supports packages, writes custom code, and fixes issues automatically.  \\n- \u2601\ufe0f **Unified Local & Cloud projects** \u2014 no more choosing between them. You\u2019ll get deploy, simulator testing, and hybrid workflows in one.  \\n- \ud83c\udfa8 Any **AI output will soon be fully visually modifiable**, giving you total creative control.  \\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **New tutorials**: building a **Movie App** and a **Mental Health App** using Supabase + ChatGPT.  \\n- \ud83d\udcd8 **Brand-new Docs** for Nowa 3.0.  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you encounter any issues, please report them using the **in-app Feedback** button \u2014 it helps us resolve problems faster."},{"id":"3-0-6","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-6","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-09-09-3-0-6.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.6: Stability fixes","description":"Nowa 3.0.6 is a stability-focused release, fixing several important issues to make building, previewing, and deploying your projects more reliable.","date":"2025-09-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.6: Stability fixes","sidebar_label":"3.0.6 \xb7 Stability fixes","description":"Nowa 3.0.6 is a stability-focused release, fixing several important issues to make building, previewing, and deploying your projects more reliable.","slug":"3-0-6","date":"2025-09-09T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.8: New templates","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-8"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.4: A more reliable AI agent","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-4"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0.6 is a stability-focused release, fixing several important issues to make building, previewing, and deploying your projects more reliable.  \\nCheck all fixes in the [ChangeLog](/new/change-log#306-8-september-2025).  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\nWe\u2019re preparing fresh resources and features to help you get the most out of Nowa 3.0:  \\n\\n- \ud83c\udfa5 **Video Tutorial:** Build a full AI-powered app with ChatGPT + Supabase that collects your mood and feelings, then analyzes them like an expert.  \\n- \ud83c\udfac **Video Tutorial:** Build a beautiful Movie App from scratch using APIs.  \\n- \ud83d\udcd8 **New Docs** for Nowa 3.0 with a clearer structure and guides.  \\n- \u26a1 **Live Streaming AI Results** \u2014 watch the AI generate results in real time inside the builder.  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you encounter any issues, please report them using the **Feedback** button inside Nowa. This helps us quickly track and resolve problems."},{"id":"3-0-4","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-4","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-08-29-3-0-4.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.4: A more reliable AI agent","description":"Nowa 3.0.4 is a stability-focused release that resolves several important issues and makes the AI agent more reliable. Alongside the fixes, we\u2019ve also added new learning resources to help you explore what\u2019s possible with Nowa 3.0.","date":"2025-08-29T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.4: A more reliable AI agent","sidebar_label":"3.0.4 \xb7 A more reliable AI agent","description":"Nowa 3.0.4 is a stability-focused release that resolves several important issues and makes the AI agent more reliable. Alongside the fixes, we\u2019ve also added new learning resources to help you explore what\u2019s possible with Nowa 3.0.","slug":"3-0-4","date":"2025-08-29T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.6: Stability fixes","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-6"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.2: Stability fixes","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-2"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0.4 is a stability-focused release that resolves several important issues and makes the AI agent more reliable. Alongside the fixes, we\u2019ve also added **new learning resources** to help you explore what\u2019s possible with Nowa 3.0.  \\nCheck all details on the [ChangeLog](/new/change-log#304-29-august-2025).  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## **New Learning Resources \ud83d\udcda**  \\n\\n\ud83c\udfa7 **Build a Music Player with Nowa 3.0 Agent**  \\nStep-by-step video tutorial showing how to create a music player app powered by the AI agent.  \\n**[Watch here \u2192](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kXfqaZSzG0g)**  \\n\\n\ud83d\udcdd **Build a To-Do App with Supabase**  \\nLearn how to connect Supabase Auth and database tables in Nowa to create a functional to-do app.  \\n**[Read the blog \u2192](https://blog.nowa.dev/build-todo-app-with-supabase-nowa-3)**  \\n\\n\ud83e\udde0 **Master Prompting with Nowa AI**  \\nA practical guide to writing prompts that produce accurate, connected, and production-ready results.  \\n**[Explore the guide \u2192](https://blog.nowa.dev/nowa-ai-prompting-guide)**  \\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n\\nWe\u2019re preparing a series of **fully functional app tutorials**, including:  \\n- \ud83d\udcb8 Financial Tracker App  \\n- \ud83c\udfcb\ufe0f Workout Planner App  \\n- \ud83e\udd16 AI-Powered Chat App  \\n- \ud83d\udcdd Note-Taking App with Supabase  \\n\\nThese apps will be released in the coming days, complete with **step-by-step tutorials** so you can build them too.  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f Don\u2019t forget to use the **Feedback button** for any ideas or issues \u2014 it helps us make Nowa better for you."},{"id":"3-0-2","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-2","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-08-12-3-0-2.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.2: Stability fixes","description":"Nowa 3.0.2 is a stability-focused update, fixing several important issues to make building, deploying, and loading your projects more reliable.","date":"2025-08-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.2: Stability fixes","sidebar_label":"3.0.2 \xb7 Stability fixes","description":"Nowa 3.0.2 is a stability-focused update, fixing several important issues to make building, deploying, and loading your projects more reliable.","slug":"3-0-2","date":"2025-08-12T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.4: A more reliable AI agent","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-4"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.1: Improved stability","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-1"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0.2 is a stability-focused update, fixing several important issues to make building, deploying, and loading your projects more reliable. Check them on [ChangeLog](/new/change-log#302-12-august-2025)"},{"id":"3-0-1","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-1","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-08-11-3-0-1.md","title":"Nowa 3.0.1: Improved stability","description":"Nowa 3.0.1 focuses on improving stability, fixing key issues, and adding new resources to help you get the most from Nowa AI.","date":"2025-08-11T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.1: Improved stability","sidebar_label":"3.0.1 \xb7 Improved stability","description":"Nowa 3.0.1 focuses on improving stability, fixing key issues, and adding new resources to help you get the most from Nowa AI.","slug":"3-0-1","date":"2025-08-11T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.2: Stability fixes","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-2"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0 beta: An AI agent for building, editing and debugging","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-beta"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0.1 focuses on **improving stability, fixing key issues, and adding new resources** to help you get the most from Nowa AI.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#301-11-august-2025).\\n\\n## **Fixes & Improvements \ud83d\udee0**  \\n\\n\ud83d\udcbb **Desktop App Access Restored**  \\nThe desktop version is now correctly available for all plans.  \\n\\n\ud83d\udcc4 **Board Naming Fixed**  \\nNew boards now use the name you assign \u2014 no more generic `board*.board` names.  \\n\\n\ud83c\udf4f **AI on macOS Restored**  \\nResolved an issue where AI wouldn\u2019t run on certain macOS versions due to file creation errors.  \\n\\n## **New Learning Resource \ud83d\udcda**  \\n\ud83d\udcdd **How to Write Prompts That Build Better with Nowa AI**  \\nLearn practical techniques to get **more accurate, connected, and production-ready results** from your AI agent.  \\n**[Read the guide \u2192](https://blog.nowa.dev/nowa-ai-prompting-guide)**  \\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n\ud83c\udfa5 **Video Tutorial:** Building a **Music Player App** from scratch with Nowa AI, using Supabase/API as data sources.  \\n\ud83d\udcdd **Blog:** A deep dive on how to use the **Nowa AI agent** effectively.  \\n\ud83e\udd1d **Cobuild & Launch:** We\u2019ll help you **build and launch** your app \u2014 from idea to production.  \\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f If you encounter any issues, please report them using the **in-app Feedback** button. Including your project (and AI history if relevant) gives us the best context to fix them quickly."},{"id":"3-0-beta","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-beta","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-08-04-3-0-beta.md","title":"Nowa 3.0 beta: An AI agent for building, editing and debugging","description":"Nowa 3.0 is our biggest release ever \u2014 packed with powerful AI features, backend upgrades, and a refreshed builder experience.","date":"2025-08-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Nowa AI","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/nowa-ai","description":"Releases that changed Nowa AI, its modes and the agents that work with Nowa."},{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Account and teams","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/account","description":"Releases that changed your account, workspaces, organizations and the dashboard."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 3.0 beta: An AI agent for building, editing and debugging","sidebar_label":"3.0 beta \xb7 An AI agent for building, editing and debugging","description":"Nowa 3.0 is our biggest release ever \u2014 packed with powerful AI features, backend upgrades, and a refreshed builder experience.","slug":"3-0-beta","date":"2025-08-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["nowa-ai","integrations","design","account"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0.1: Improved stability","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.21: One-click API imports","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-21"}},"content":"Nowa 3.0 is our biggest release ever \u2014 packed with powerful AI features, backend upgrades, and a refreshed builder experience. Let\u2019s dive into what\u2019s new!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#300-beta-4-august-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**\\n\\n\ud83e\udd16 **AI Agent for Building, Editing, and Debugging**  \\nGenerate entire screens, features, or app flows with a single prompt.  \\nYou can now:\\n- Build new widgets and screens instantly\\n- Edit or fix parts of your app with or without selecting anything\\n- Prompt across multiple screens \u2014 the AI understands what to connect\\n\\n\ud83d\udee0 **Supabase Integration (Beta)**  \\nBuild full-stack apps faster with native Supabase support:\\n- Authenticate users with **Supabase Auth**\\n- Use AI to generate queries\\n- Enable **row-level security** for production-ready apps\\n\\n\ud83c\udfa8 **Redesigned Theme System**  \\nAccess the new theme editor from the left bar.  \\nCreate, preview, and manage design tokens visually \u2014 no more guesswork when styling your app.\\n\\n\ud83e\udded **Upgraded Builder Experience**  \\nEnjoy a smoother and more powerful editing experience:\\n- Visual **Component Explorer** \u2014 inspect and highlight widgets across your app\\n- Improved **Boards** \u2014 navigate your screens with better layout and structure\\n\\n## **Plans & Access \ud83d\udcbc**\\n\\nWe\u2019ve made our pricing more accessible \u2014 with powerful features available to everyone.\\n\\n\ud83c\udd93 **Free Plan (Starter)**  \\n- Unlimited code exports  \\n- Unlimited projects  \\n- Desktop version + local development  \\n- Web publishing for 12h (testing)  \\n- 5 AI messages/month  \\n\\n\ud83d\ude80 **Launch & Scale Plans**  \\n- Up to **200 AI messages/month**  \\n- Web & mobile deployment  \\n- GitHub integration  \\n- Premium support  \\n- AI credit top-ups\\n\\n\ud83c\udf81 **Bonus for Existing Users:**  \\n- Pro users now get 35 AI messages/month  \\n- Premium users now get full **Scale Plan** access at the original price\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**\\n\\n\ud83c\udfa5 **Tutorial Video:** Watch how to build a full app using the new AI agent  \\n\ud83d\udcdd **Pricing Blog Post:** See what\u2019s included in each plan, with clear use cases  \\n\ud83e\udd1d **Cobuild & Launch (for Scale users):** Our team helps you build and launch your app \u2014 step-by-step, no extra cost\\n\\n\u27a1\ufe0f Found a bug in the BETA? Report it using the in-app Feedback button and earn **extra AI credits** as a thank you!"},{"id":"2-0-21","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-21","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-05-27-2-0-21.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.21: One-click API imports","description":"This update makes managing APIs faster than ever, squashes critical bugs, and sets the stage for the AI-powered future of Nowa.","date":"2025-05-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.21: One-click API imports","sidebar_label":"2.0.21 \xb7 One-click API imports","description":"This update makes managing APIs faster than ever, squashes critical bugs, and sets the stage for the AI-powered future of Nowa.","slug":"2-0-21","date":"2025-05-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 3.0 beta: An AI agent for building, editing and debugging","permalink":"/new/whats-new/3-0-beta"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.20: An all-new API editor","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-20"}},"content":"This update makes managing APIs faster than ever, squashes critical bugs, and sets the stage for the AI-powered future of Nowa. Let\u2019s dive in!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2021-27-may-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n\ud83d\udce6 **One-Click API Imports**  \\nSkip the manual setup! Import groups of API requests instantly from:\\n- **Postman**\\n- **Swagger**\\n- **Xano**\\n\\nSimply import, and Nowa automatically handles the rest\u2014endpoints, request types, headers, and body included.\\n\\nFor more, check out [this page](/integrations/rest-api/import)\\n\\n\ud83d\udce5 **Instant cURL Support**  \\nPaste a **cURL command**, and Nowa turns it into a ready-to-use API request. Less manual work, more building!\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n\ud83e\udd16 **AI Assistant (Alpha testing already going!)**  \\nWe\u2019ve begun private alpha testing for our AI Assistant. Soon, you\u2019ll effortlessly:\\n- Generate entire apps or screens instantly with prompting  \\n- Edit existing screens and components, and prompt to fix bugs or unexpected behaviours.  \\n- Connect APIs seamlessly through AI-powered logic.  \\n\\nThe early results are astonishing\u2014combining visual editing and AI is proving incredibly fast and powerful!\\n\\n\ud83d\udc49 [Sign Up for Early Access](https://forms.gle/xNUR7nsYRUz8kpJ67)"},{"id":"2-0-20","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-20","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-04-23-2-0-20.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.20: An all-new API editor","description":"This update brings a whole new API workflow, smarter debugging in Play mode, and better defaults across the board. Let\u2019s dig in!","date":"2025-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Integrations","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/integrations","description":"Releases that changed APIs, Supabase, Firebase, payments, maps and other services."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."},{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.20: An all-new API editor","sidebar_label":"2.0.20 \xb7 An all-new API editor","description":"This update brings a whole new API workflow, smarter debugging in Play mode, and better defaults across the board. Let\u2019s dig in!","slug":"2-0-20","date":"2025-04-23T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["integrations","logic","preview","design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.21: One-click API imports","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-21"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.19: Nowa Marketplace","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-19"}},"content":"This update brings a whole new API workflow, smarter debugging in Play mode, and better defaults across the board. Let\u2019s dig in!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2020-23-april-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n\ud83e\udde9 **All-New API Editor**  \\nManaging your APIs just got way more powerful:\\n- View and manage **all requests in one place**, right next to your files  \\n- A streamlined flow for creating, testing, and generating models/mock data  \\n- Supports **form data**\u2014so you can now handle **file uploads** easily  \\n- Control over **content-type** for each request  \\n\\n\ud83d\udccf **Smarter Padding Controls**  \\nAdd **Horizontal** and **Vertical** padding directly\u2014cut down the typing, boost your layout precision!\\n\\n\u25b6\ufe0f **Play Panel, Upgraded**  \\nWhile testing your app in Play mode, you can now **select elements directly**\u2014making UI debugging a breeze.\\n\\n\ud83d\udcac **Chat Template Gets a Boost**  \\nWe gave our built-in Chat template some love:\\n- **Profile component** added for a personal touch  \\n- **App Bar** now included with account info  \\n- Input validation prevents sending empty messages  \\n- Improved naming and structure for easier edits  \\n\\n\ud83d\udd0d **Better Logic Building in Circuit**  \\n- Hover on any function to see its **return type**  \\n- The **search** now includes all **main nodes**, so you find what you need faster\\n\\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Play Mode Custom Code Warning**  \\nGot custom functions or widgets? You\u2019ll now see a **warning** when using Play mode, so you know it may use dummy values unless tested on a simulator.\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n- \ud83e\udd16 **AI-generated expressions** \u2014 just describe what you need, and let AI handle the logic  \\n- \ud83d\udcd8 **AI-powered Docs Assistant** to help you find answers instantly (currently in BETA)  \\n- Even more **API upgrades**  \\n- And\u2026 something **BIG** is coming soon \ud83d\udc40"},{"id":"2-0-19","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-19","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-04-06-2-0-19.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.19: Nowa Marketplace","description":"Nowa Marketplace is finally here! This update brings you a faster way to build with sample projects, a powerful Git integration, a fresh button widget, and better error handling\u2014all designed to supercharge your workflow.","date":"2025-04-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.19: Nowa Marketplace","sidebar_label":"2.0.19 \xb7 Nowa Marketplace","description":"Nowa Marketplace is finally here! This update brings you a faster way to build with sample projects, a powerful Git integration, a fresh button widget, and better error handling\u2014all designed to supercharge your workflow.","slug":"2-0-19","date":"2025-04-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.20: An all-new API editor","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-20"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.18: Chat template","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-18"}},"content":"Nowa Marketplace is finally here! \ud83d\ude80 This update brings you a faster way to build with sample projects, a powerful Git integration, a fresh button widget, and better error handling\u2014all designed to supercharge your workflow.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2019-6-april-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**\\n\\n\ud83d\udecd\ufe0f **Nowa Marketplace**  \\nIntroducing our very first **Marketplace**\u2014your new starting point to build faster with real, editable projects:\\n- Discover sample apps right from the dashboard  \\n- Preview them, check the structure, and **Add App** to start building  \\n- View details like APIs, AI, and custom code setups  \\n\\nWe\u2019re launching with:  \\n- \ud83e\uddca **Water Tracker App** \u2013 featured in [our latest tutorial](https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLVhnHv8Cdhz87lklVjSao4Y0EHdlq2j5a)  \\n- \ud83e\udd16 **AI Chat App** \u2013 a complete ChatGPT-powered messaging experience\\n\\n\ud83d\udd01 **Revamped Git Integration**  \\nManage your projects like a pro with full Git operations:\\n- Clone from any Git provider (like GitHub)  \\n- Push cloud projects to Git  \\n- Keep local, cloud, and remote versions in sync  \\n- Commit, discard, branch\u2014you name it  \\n[Check out the full Git guide](/code/git)\\n\\n\ud83d\udd18 **New Button Widget**  \\nCustomize your buttons with the all-new `ButtonStyle`:\\n- Set background color, text style, border radius, elevation, and more  \\n- Apply a `ButtonTheme` across your app for consistent styling\\n\\n\u26a0\ufe0f **Smarter Error Handling**  \\n- Get warnings before layout issues happen  \\n- Prevent actions that could crash your app  \\n- Quickly spot and fix problems with **file-specific error messages**\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n\ud83c\udf6f Easier API workflows  \\n\ud83d\udd01 Big improvements to Circuit  \\n\ud83d\udcf1 More sample projects  \\n\ud83c\udfa5 Tutorial on building advanced features in the AI Chat App\\n\\n## **New learning resources**\\nWe\u2019ve added new docs to help you learn and master building with Nowa:\\n\\n### \ud83e\uddec Hybrid Approach\\n- [\ud83c\udf3f Intro to Hybrid Approach](/code/vs-code)  \\n- [\ud83e\udde9 Using Custom Code](/code/custom-code)  \\n\\n### \ud83e\udde0 Circuit & Logic\\n- [\ud83d\udd0c Circuit Intro](/logic/circuit)  \\n- [\ud83d\udd00 If Statement](/logic/conditions)  \\n- [\ud83e\uddef Try Catch](/logic/conditions)  \\n\\n### \ud83e\udded Common Functionalities\\n- [\ud83e\udded Navigation](/logic/navigation)  \\n- [\ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f Media Picker](/logic/popups)  \\n- [\ud83d\udcbb Check Platform](/logic/actions)  \\n- [\ud83d\udda8\ufe0f Print](/logic/actions)  \\n\\n### \ud83d\udce6 Variables & States\\n- [\ud83e\udde0 Using Data Models](/logic/models)  \\n- [\ud83c\udf0d Global States](/logic/global-state)  \\n\\n### \ud83d\udd01 Git & Version Control\\n- [\ud83d\udd01 Full Git & GitHub Guide](/code/git)"},{"id":"2-0-18","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-18","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-03-12-2-0-18.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.18: Chat template","description":"This update introduces our newest built-in template\u2014AI Chat\u2014allowing you to quickly build your own chat-based apps. Plus, we\'ve made navigating your project logic faster and easier!","date":"2025-03-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.18: Chat template","sidebar_label":"2.0.18 \xb7 Chat template","description":"This update introduces our newest built-in template\u2014AI Chat\u2014allowing you to quickly build your own chat-based apps. Plus, we\'ve made navigating your project logic faster and easier!","slug":"2-0-18","date":"2025-03-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","logic"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.19: Nowa Marketplace","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-19"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.17: Web deployment","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-17"}},"content":"This update introduces our newest built-in template\u2014**AI Chat**\u2014allowing you to quickly build your own chat-based apps. Plus, we\'ve made navigating your project logic faster and easier!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2018-beta-12-march-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n\ud83e\udd16 **Chat Template**  \\nNowa now includes an **Chat template**, helping you to quickly create a powerful chat experiences in your app:\\n- Ready-to-use **chat screen** for immediate integration.\\n- Pre-built components including **chat bubbles** and **chat logic**.\\n- Fully customizable to fit your own chat use case!\\n[See how to use it here](/legacy/tutorials/chat-template)\\n\\n\ud83d\ude80 **Quick Navigation to Functions & APIs**  \\nWe\'ve enhanced your workflow in Circuit with **quick navigation**:\\n- Click the new **\\"open\\" icon** next to functions or API request nodes.\\n- Instantly jump directly to the source, making edits easier and faster.\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n- **Sample Projects**: AI Chatbot, To-Do app, and a Water Tracker App!"},{"id":"2-0-17","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-17","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-03-04-2-0-17.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.17: Web deployment","description":"This update introduces a major new capability\u2014Web Deployment\u2014allowing you to publish and share your web apps with a single click.","date":"2025-03-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Publish","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/publish","description":"Releases that changed deploying to the web and getting into the App Store and Google Play."},{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.17: Web deployment","sidebar_label":"2.0.17 \xb7 Web deployment","description":"This update introduces a major new capability\u2014Web Deployment\u2014allowing you to publish and share your web apps with a single click.","slug":"2-0-17","date":"2025-03-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["publish","design"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.18: Chat template","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-18"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.15: Swipeable Stack and Time Picker","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-15"}},"content":"This update introduces a major new capability\u2014**Web Deployment**\u2014allowing you to **publish and share your web apps with a single click**. Plus, we\'ve added **new widgets**, improved the dashboard, and enhanced audio support!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2017-beta-5-march-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n- **Web Deployment**  \\n  Nowa now allows you to **deploy your web apps online effortlessly**. You can choose between:\\n  - **Development Mode**: Share a temporary link for testing, available for all users.\\n  - **Production Mode**: Publish a **permanent live version** (Pro & Premium users only) and even use a **custom domain**.\\n  - Need to host it yourself? **Download the build files** and deploy them anywhere!\\n\\nCheck out the **[full guide on web deployment](/publish/web)** to get started!\\n\\n- **Badge Wrapper**  \\n  Introducing the `Badge` wrapper\u2014perfect for displaying **small notifications, labels, or indicators** in your UI. Easily **customize colors, shapes, and text** to highlight important elements.\\n\\n- **Pin Code Field Widget**  \\n  Need to collect **secure PIN inputs**? The new `Pin Code Field` widget allows users to enter PINs or OTP codes with a customizable look and feel.\\n\\n## **Improvements \ud83d\udd27**  \\n\\n- **Dashboard Enhancements**  \\n  - We\u2019ve **separated cloud projects from local projects**, making it easier to manage your workspace and distinguish between them.\\n\\n- **Audio Source Enhancements**  \\n  - Nowa now supports **playing audio directly from bytes**, giving you more flexibility when handling audio playback.\\n\\n- **Request Templates Directly from the Panel**  \\n  - Need a specific app template? You can now **request templates directly** from inside the Nowa panel, and we will work on it right away!\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n- **Sample Projects**: including a AI-Chatgot, To-Do app, and a Water Tracker App"},{"id":"2-0-15","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-15","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-02-12-2-0-15.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.15: Swipeable Stack and Time Picker","description":"This update brings exciting new widgets and important improvements to Nowa, including Swipeable Stack, Time Picker, and various bug fixes.","date":"2025-02-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.15: Swipeable Stack and Time Picker","sidebar_label":"2.0.15 \xb7 Swipeable Stack and Time Picker","description":"This update brings exciting new widgets and important improvements to Nowa, including Swipeable Stack, Time Picker, and various bug fixes.","slug":"2-0-15","date":"2025-02-12T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","logic"],"image":"/img/whats_new/swipingcard.gif"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.17: Web deployment","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-17"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.13: Git integration for cloud projects","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-13"}},"content":"This update brings exciting new widgets and important improvements to Nowa, including **Swipeable Stack**, **Time Picker**, and various bug fixes.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2015-beta-12-feb-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n- **Swipeable Stack Widget**  \\n  Nowa now supports **Tinder-style swiping cards**! Use the `Swipeable Stack` widget to create **interactive swipe effects** for card-based UIs. Simply **connect it to a list variable**, just like ListView, and bring a dynamic experience to your app.  \\n\\n- **Time Picker**  \\n  You can now allow users to **select a specific time** in your app! Previously, Nowa only supported picking dates. With `ShowTimePicker`, you can capture user input for time selection and format it easily using `.format()`.  \\n\\n  ![](/img/whats_new/swipingcard.gif)\\n\\n## **Coming Soon \ud83d\udd1c**  \\n\\n- **Web Hosting with Custom Domains**  \\n  Host your **Flutter web apps** directly from Nowa and set up a **custom domain** in just a few clicks.  \\n\\n- **AI Voice Assistant App Template**  \\n  Get a pre-built **real-time AI voice assistant** template, ready to be customized with your own API keys and settings.  \\n\\n- **VS Code Integration (Planned)**  \\n  Work with Nowa **inside VS Code** for a seamless hybrid workflow, combining **visual building and coding** in one place."},{"id":"2-0-13","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-13","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-02-04-2-0-13.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.13: Git integration for cloud projects","description":"This update brings major improvements to Nowa, including Git integration, media picking, account management, and a new package management system.","date":"2025-02-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."},{"inline":false,"label":"Account and teams","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/account","description":"Releases that changed your account, workspaces, organizations and the dashboard."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.13: Git integration for cloud projects","sidebar_label":"2.0.13 \xb7 Git integration for cloud projects","description":"This update brings major improvements to Nowa, including Git integration, media picking, account management, and a new package management system.","slug":"2-0-13","date":"2025-02-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["code","logic","account"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.15: Swipeable Stack and Time Picker","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-15"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.14: A new dashboard design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-14"}},"content":"This update brings major improvements to Nowa, including **Git integration**, **media picking**, **account management**, and a **new package management system**.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2013-beta-4-feb-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n- **Git Integration for Cloud Projects (Web & Windows)**  \\n  Connect your Nowa cloud project to **GitHub (or any Git service)** to **commit, push, pull, switch branches**, and more. You can also **link local projects to the cloud** for the best of both worlds\u2014**hot-reload & hybrid approach locally + one-click deployment in the cloud**. *(MacOS support coming soon!)*  \\n\\n- **Media Picker**  \\n  You can now **select media files** inside your app and **upload them through an API with encoding** for more dynamic experiences.  \\n\\n- **Account Management**  \\n  Customize your profile by updating your **name, profile picture, email, and password**. You can also **delete your account** if needed.  \\n\\n- **Package Management System**  \\n  View, add, remove, and update all **packages in your project** effortlessly from one place."},{"id":"2-0-14","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-14","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-01-29-2-0-14.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.14: A new dashboard design","description":"This update brings a brand-new dashboard design and support for the Intl package for date/time formatting, improving both usability and localization capabilities.","date":"2025-01-29T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Account and teams","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/account","description":"Releases that changed your account, workspaces, organizations and the dashboard."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.14: A new dashboard design","sidebar_label":"2.0.14 \xb7 A new dashboard design","description":"This update brings a brand-new dashboard design and support for the Intl package for date/time formatting, improving both usability and localization capabilities.","slug":"2-0-14","date":"2025-01-29T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["account","logic"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.13: Git integration for cloud projects","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-13"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.11: Expansion Tile widget","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-11"}},"content":"This update brings a **brand-new dashboard design** and support for the **Intl package for date/time formatting**, improving both usability and localization capabilities.  \\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2014-29-jan-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n\\n- **New Dashboard Design**  \\n  We\u2019ve redesigned the dashboard for a **smoother and more intuitive experience**.  \\n  - Easily navigate between **projects and workspaces**.  \\n  - Discover the **new Learning Resources section**, where you\u2019ll find top guides, tutorials, and tips to **help you build faster and better**.  \\n\\n- **Intl Package for Date/Time Formatting**  \\n  Nowa now supports the **Intl package in Flutter**, allowing you to:  \\n  - **Format dates, times, and numbers** based on locale preferences.  \\n  - Easily localize your app with **region-specific date formats, timezone adjustments, currency formatting, and pluralization rules**."},{"id":"2-0-11","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-11","source":"@site/whats-new/2025-01-06-2-0-11.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.11: Expansion Tile widget","description":"This version introduces powerful new features, improvements, and essential bug fixes to enhance your experience.","date":"2025-01-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.11: Expansion Tile widget","sidebar_label":"2.0.11 \xb7 Expansion Tile widget","description":"This version introduces powerful new features, improvements, and essential bug fixes to enhance your experience.","slug":"2-0-11","date":"2025-01-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.14: A new dashboard design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-14"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.10: Play mode on the board","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-10"}},"content":"This version introduces powerful new features, improvements, and essential bug fixes to enhance your experience.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2011-beta-7-jan-2025).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**  \\n- **Expansion Tile Widget:**  \\n  Add collapsible sections in your app with the new Expansion Tile widget. Perfect for organizing content hierarchically.  \\n  [Learn more](/reference/widgets#expansion-tile)  \\n\\n- **Getters in the Hybrid Approach:**  \\n  Write custom Getters in code and use them seamlessly in your project for more flexibility in app logic.  \\n\\n- **TextField Theming:**  \\n  Define a global style for TextFields in your app theme, saving time on repetitive UI customizations. Your TextFields will automatically align with the app theme."},{"id":"2-0-10","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-10","source":"@site/whats-new/2024-12-16-2-0-10.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.10: Play mode on the board","description":"This version comes with important enhancements and fixes to make your experience easier and more powerful.","date":"2024-12-16T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Preview and test","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/preview","description":"Releases that changed Instant Play, Run, sharing and testing on your devices."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.10: Play mode on the board","sidebar_label":"2.0.10 \xb7 Play mode on the board","description":"This version comes with important enhancements and fixes to make your experience easier and more powerful.","slug":"2-0-10","date":"2024-12-16T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["preview","logic"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.11: Expansion Tile widget","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-11"},"nextItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.8 beta: Nowa V2 is here","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-8-beta"}},"content":"This version comes with important enhancements and fixes to make your experience easier and more powerful.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#2010-beta-16-dec-2024).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**\\n- Play Mode on the Board: Run your app directly from the board without entering file preview. Select a screen and hit Play. If no screen is selected, the app starts from the Home screen.\\n- Variables Panel on the Board: Create variables, parameters, and functions right from the board\u2014no need to enter file preview.\\n- Local Variables in Functions: Easily create local variables within functions. Right-click inside Circuit and select \u201cCreate Local Variable\u201d to scope it to the function.\\n- Store Expression Results in Existing Variables: When using \u201cCustom Expression\u201d in Circuit, you can now store the result in an existing variable. Just choose \u201cPick Variable\u201d next to \u201cStore Results.\u201d\\n- Added Compute Option: Use \u201cCompute\u201d to create a function that computes the value of a field, just like in Version 1.\\n- Upgraded to Flutter 3.27: Your apps now run on the latest Flutter version for better performance and compatibility."},{"id":"2-0-8-beta","metadata":{"permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-8-beta","source":"@site/whats-new/2024-11-28-2-0-8-beta.md","title":"Nowa 2.0.8 beta: Nowa V2 is here","description":"Nowa V2 is here! After 7 weeks of exclusive testing with hand-picked users, we\u2019re happy to open Nowa V2 to everyone!","date":"2024-11-28T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Design","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/design","description":"Releases that changed the board, widgets, themes, templates and the Library."},{"inline":false,"label":"Logic","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/logic","description":"Releases that changed Circuit, variables, functions and navigation."},{"inline":false,"label":"Code and Git","permalink":"/new/whats-new/tags/code","description":"Releases that changed working with code, packages, local projects and Git."}],"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[],"frontMatter":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.8 beta: Nowa V2 is here","sidebar_label":"2.0.8 beta \xb7 Nowa V2 is here","description":"Nowa V2 is here! After 7 weeks of exclusive testing with hand-picked users, we\u2019re happy to open Nowa V2 to everyone!","slug":"2-0-8-beta","date":"2024-11-28T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["design","logic","code"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Nowa 2.0.10: Play mode on the board","permalink":"/new/whats-new/2-0-10"}},"content":"Nowa V2 is here! After 7 weeks of exclusive testing with hand-picked users, we\u2019re happy to open Nowa V2 to everyone!\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\nThis version introduces groundbreaking new features, an improved workflow, and an enhanced overall experience. Let\u2019s dive into the details.\\n\\n\ud83d\udccb Check all the details of this release in the [changelog](/new/change-log#208-beta-28-nov-2024).\\n\\n## **New \u2728**\\n\\n- **A Unified Workflow:** The new workflow eliminates friction, allowing seamless navigation and improved productivity throughout the app-building process. Here\'s some of the new improvements on the workflow:\\n\\n  - **UI Boards:** Organize all your UIs on visual boards for a clear overview of your project.\\n  - **Focused File Tabs:** Open individual files in their own tabs, allowing you to fully focus on specific components.\\n  - **Declaration Navigation:** For files with multiple declarations (e.g., multiple widgets), use the declaration chips on the bottom-left panel to switch between them effortlessly.\\n  - **Isolated Screen Testing:** Play an isolated screen directly from the file preview to test its behavior in isolation.\\n  - **Code View:** Access the code for any file by clicking `Code` on the bottom-left panel.\\n  - **Declaration Map:** While in code preview, view a mapped structure of all declarations in the left-side panel for easier navigation and understanding.\\n\\n- **Custom Code Support:** Write custom Flutter code anywhere in your project, including functions, widgets, and classes. Modify the generated code, and see changes sync instantly inside Nowa. For more, [watch this video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hlOoXTdw1vg&t=1087s)\\n- **Themes Management:** Create and manage multiple themes for your app, customize colors and typography, and dynamically switch themes during runtime. [Read more about it here](/design/themes)\\n- **Revamped Logic-Building Circuit:** Build more complex and advanced flows with the new Circuit. Features include:\\n  - \\"Await\\" for asynchronous functions.\\n  - \\"Try-Catch\\" support for functions that may throw exceptions (e.g., network requests).\\n  - Using Custom Expressions \\n- **Advanced Expressions:** Write advanced Dart expressions directly in the UI Designer or Circuit. Use the new Advanced Expression Builder to create:\\n  - Conditional, mathematical, null-aware, and boolean expressions.\\n- **Integrated Flutter Development:** Instantly sync changes between Nowa and your local Flutter development environment.\\n- **New File System:** Organize your project with ease:\\n  - **Dart File Navigation:** Seamlessly navigate between your project\u2019s Dart files for a more structured workflow.\\n  - **File Previewer:** Preview all Dart files in your project with an intuitive interface.\\n  - **Dedicated Sections:** Access distinct sections for UI boards, Dart files, and assets, keeping everything organized and easy to locate.\\n- **Enhanced File Previewer:** View and navigate through your project\u2019s Dart files with the new file previewer.\\n- **Improved Widgets:** Enhanced customization options and functionality for a smoother design experience.\\n- **Significant Code Quality Improvements:** The generated Flutter code is cleaner, more performant, and better structured.\\n\\n## **What\u2019s Coming Soon \ud83d\ude80**\\n\\n- **New Documentation and Tutorials:** Updated tutorials and documentation tailored for Nowa V2.\\n- **Upcoming Video Tutorials:**\\n  - Detailed onboarding for Nowa V2.\\n  - A full walkthrough to build a water reminder app.\\n- **Frequent Livestreams:** Get insights, tips, and interact with the Nowa team in regular live streams.\\n- **Hackathon:** Participate in our upcoming hackathon for a chance to win exciting prizes.\\n\\n## New Learning Resources \ud83d\udcda\\n\\n- [Nowa V2 Playlist](https://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLVhnHv8Cdhz8rAHO0Z-xdUmATgB91458t&si=YXy_9oAzLmC-57Wx): Explore Nowa V2 with our new Youtube playlist for Nowa V2."}]}}')}}]);